1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He lived and died in this area. His will named son Jacob as administrator. No burial record is found. His wife Christina was living with him in 1820
2 CONT
2 CONT PETER KEHLINCrER or KEPLINGER or HSHLINCffiR - S. 39684
2 CONT
2 CONT Nov. 9, 1818 - personally appeared Peter Keblinger aged 62 years a resident of Brecknock Township, Berks County that he enlisted in the service of the United States in the year 1778 in a company commanded by
2 CONT Capt. Ceorge Grant for three years, ninth Pennsylvania Regiment, Col. Butler, that he remained with the service aforesaid during the term of his enlistment, that he had received an lionorable Discharge from Col. Butler which is lo
2 CONC st. That he about twelve years since received a stroke of Palsey whereby he has lost the use of his left arm. That he has received no pension (under the laws of the U.S.). That he is poor and in reduced circumstances.
2 CONT Peter (x) Keblinger
2 CONT November 9, 1818 - appeared Nicholas Burkhart of Robeson Township who swears knowing Peter Keblinger upwards of 10 years and swears to facts.
2 CONT Nicholas Burfchart (German)
2 CONT District of Pennsylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT August 8, 1820 - Peter Keblinger aged 63, Certificate no. 6414.
2 CONT
2 CONT Schedule of Property- Peter Keblinger, no family residing with him except wife Christina, aged 7E, infirm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pension of $50 a year from State of Pennsylvania.
