1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See pages 7 & 8... https://www.yumpu.com/en/document/read/3679546/family-tree-maker
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genforum.genealogy.com/propst/messages/205.html
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1784, in Anson Co, NC, Catharine Abendschon married Heinrich Propst, a well known doctor in that area. Catharine's father was Christian Abendschon whose father was Samuel Heinrich Abendschon.
2 CONT
2 CONT I've just seen a query in the listing for Berks Co, PA, regarding Samuel ancestry. I've attached it since it provides a listing of Samuel's ancestors for six generations, something I'd not seen before. If any of you can help Vicki
2 CONC  Rock Payne, I'm sure she'd be grateful.
2 CONT --------
2 CONT Subject: Abendschon/Abendtschon/Auvenshine From: Vicki R Payne <vpayne@highland.net>
2 CONT
2 CONT Hi, I am looking for any connections to the Abendschon family descending from:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wendel Abendschon (b. abt 1512 - d. abt. 1612) Germany Hans Abendschon (b. abt. 1587 - d. 1637) Germany Johannes Abendschon (b. 01/20/1626-27 - d. 02/28/1684-85) Schwaigern, Germany Wolfgang Phillipp Abendschon (05/23/1655 - d.12/
2 CONC 04/1726) Wuerttemberg, Germany Samuel Heinrich Abendschon b. 08/24/1685, Schwaigern, Germany, d. 10/27/1756, Berks County, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT My files show the following continuation:
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian Abendschon, b 1716, d 1793, m Anna Catharina Behringer. Catharine Abendschon, b 1757, d 1845, m Heinrich Propst, MD
