2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/105927299/jacob-hammer
2 CONT
2 CONT Died at his home, February 4, 1898, Mr. Jacob Hammer, aged 76 years, 11 months, and 12 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Born in Pendleton County W.Va, on February 22, 1821, he was the son of George and Catharine Hammer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  In early manhood he married Miss. Timna Conrad of the same county, who survives him, this union produced 10 children, Isaac D., Noah, who died with diphtheria during the Civil War, Howard who was killed at Fisher's Hill, Va., Jas
2 CONC . C., Sarah, now MRs. R. Dahmer, Ursula T., now Mrs. Geo. W. Hammer, Miss Deniza C., Lee, Clay, and Anna, now Mrs. I.H. Davis, were the results of the union.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He left thirteen grand children and two great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was a member of the German Baptist Church some 23 years and continued a member until his dying day.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was honest and industrious through life and had accumulated considerable wealth.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was always ready to help those in want and never permitted anyone to leave his door hungry or without being supplied with the necessaries of life when in actual need.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He had filled various important positions in his county and was always faithful on discharging his duty and looking to the interest of his native county.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Uncle Jake will be missed in the various departments of life. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thus one more landmark of the past is gone and we should profit by his good traits, and his bad ones, if he had any, let us blot out from our memory.
2 CONT
2 CONT   {Abstracted from Pendleton County Obituaries}
2 CONT
2 CONT Contributed by: Shock
