1 NAME Adam Dice /Hammer/
2 GIVN Adam Dice
2 SURN Hammer
2 _MARNM Hammer
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Hillside Cemetery (Plot Block B Lot 30)
2 ADDR
3 CITY Cedar Falls
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 14 FEB 1823
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 JUL 1888
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A.D. Hammer just east of this city, died early in the week and was buried on Tuesday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Hammer had his birth in Western Virginia in 1823. Was married in 1847 to Miss. Malinda Waggoner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Four children were born to them, two of whom were taken from earth to the "better country" a few years since.
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased, soon after his marriage, located in Ohio, from hence he moved to Cedar Falls, where he had continued to the day of his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Greatly esteemed and loved for his manifold virtues by his neighbors, he leaves his widow and two children, a son and a daughter, to sorrow but not without hope.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is no more than the facts warrant when we say that our departed brother possessed in a high degree all the virtues of the model husband, the kind and affectionate father, the thoughtful and generous citizen and the exemplary ch
2 CONC ristian. He sleeps well.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral from the residence Tuesday afternoon, by Rev. J. Bowman and was largely attended.
2 CONT
2 CONT   {Abstracted from Pendleton County Obituaries} Contributed by #47473371
