2 CONT A History of the UpperPottsgrove Township Steinruck Homestead, [by S. Duane Kauffman, 1411Schwenkmill Rd., Perkasie, PA November 24, 1973] This is a review of the realestate transactions involving the 102 acre farm between Levengo
2 CONC od Road andChestnut Grove Road in Upper Pottsgrove Township. Deeds recorded at theMontgomery County Courthouse at Norristown were used.
2 CONT         The following deed is the key. Followingis an abstract: 516-378 JOHN STEINRUCKET AL TO JOHN WEILER, APRil 2, 1824
2 CONT         BetweenJohn Steinruck and Samuel Steinruck both of Douglass Township, Berks County,executors of the last will of Christian Steinruck late of Pottstown, parties ofthe first part and John Weiler of Pottstown, the other part.
2 CONT      HISTORY OF PROPERTY TO THIS POINT
2 CONT         On March 26, 1761 the tract of 100acres, 50 perches was granted by Samuel and Mary McCall of Philadelphia toJoachim Godschalk.
2 CONT         On November 18, 1767 Joachim andElizabeth Godshalk granted the tract to George Steinruck.
2 CONT         On July 26, 1796 George and AnnaSteinruck granted the land to "their son, Christian Steinruck".
2 CONT         "Said Christian in his will ofMarch 1, 1820 instructed property to be sold by his executors, John Steinruck,Samuel Steinruck, (sons) and Peter Moser (son-in-law). Moser renounced hisresponsibility. Weiler paid $775.43 at t
2 CONC he time of purchase and $1,066.67 to bepaid immediately after the decease of BARBARA, widow and relict of said ChristianSteinruck, to the heirs of said deceased".
2 CONT      DESCRIPTION OF PROPERTY "Beginning at astone corner of John Mock's land and running thence by the same and land ofJohn Reifsnyder respectively south fifty six degreees east one hundred andeighty three perches to a post at the
2 CONC  corner of John Reifsnyder's land, Then bythe same south eighty four degrees west four perches to a post and south sixdegrees east nineteen perches to a post on corner of John Reifsnyder's (Sr.)land thence by the same south thirty
2 CONC  four degrees west sixty eight perches onehundred and ninety one perches and a half to a stone corner in a line ofChristian Gorgas' land thence by the same and land of John Mock respectivelynorth thirty four degrees east eighty si
2 CONC x perches and three tenths to the placeof beginning, containing one hundred and two acres of land and sixty fiveperches. {witnesses were William Rinehart and John Stauffer] 197-228 JOHN S. WEILERto HENRY LEVENGOOD, February 23, 18
2 CONC 43 (Levengood from Pottstown. In    descriptionChristian Yergey replaces C. Gorgas) 357-410 REBECCALEVENGOOD ET AL    (Hier of HenryLevengood) to CAROLINE Y. KEYSER, April 2, 1891
2 CONT         Ona map in the Court House Deed Room, a map of Montgomery County clearly showsthe farm identifed in her (Keyser's] name. 0-74       SHERIFF OF MONTGOMERY COUNTY to REBECCAM. LEVENGOOD, date ? (Rebecca Levengood       repur
2 CONC chased the property). 630-171 REBECCALEVENGOOD ET AL to JOHN WAHL, April 15, 1904. 670-1152 JOHN WAHL toJACOB RISCH of Wilkes Barre, April 18, 1910 781-76   JACOB RISCH to Charles L. John, March 12,1912 830-355 CHARLES L.JOHN to L
2 CONC ESLIE C. KLINE AND LESLIE BLOOM of Clearfield, PA., June 26, 1912 1190-143 SHERIFF OFMONTGOMERY COUNTY to SECURITY TRUST COMPANY OF POTTSTOWN (1934) 1205-26  SECURITY TRUST OF POTTSTOWN to ROBERT W.EVANS (Realtor) October 19, 1935
2 CONC . 1336-38  ROBERT W. EVANS to MARY THEIS, CHRISTIANTHEIS AND NICHOLAS THEIS, May 7, 1940.
2 CONT         At the present time [November 24, 1973]the farm (100 acres still intact is occupied by Mr. and Mrs. Nicholas Theis andtheir son and daughter. (Address: Rt. 20, Pottstown). The house is very old. Itis in three parts. The ol
2 CONC dest is log while the later additions are stone. Theexterior has been covered with stucco. The exterior is showing its age but theinterior is quite good and is well maintained. In my contact I found the Theisfamily to be extremely
2 CONC  amiable and cooperative! At present the property is usedas a large chicken farm.
2 CONT                     Submitted by S. DuaneKauffman, November 24, 1973.    
