2 CONT Family tradition holdsthat Samuel was the Lutheran School teacher in Boyertown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gravestones locatedbetween the Good Shepherd UCC church and the Bank property as part of the OldUnion Cemetery in Boyertown, were reinterred when both the Bank and the churchexpanded. The gravestones were mounted all together in r
2 CONC ows. Samuel'sgravestone is somewhat problematic as it contains the death date for Samuel Sr.(May 17, 1836) interposed with the birth date for Samuel Jr (September 25,1819) which creates the illusion that a 17 year old Samuel Stein
2 CONC ruck was buriedthere. There is no such Samuel Steinruck. Which Samuel, then was buried at theOld Union Cemetery in Boyertown? Logic would dictate that when burying a man,the death date would likely be correct and would apply for t
2 CONC he person beingburied and that they would have the correct date for the correct person beingburied.
2 CONT
2 CONT In this case, however,Samuel Steinruck, Jr. died in Pittsburgh, Allegheny County, PA August 20, 1859.
