2 CONT Died at Whitley Co,. IN
2 CONT
2 CONT Also seen as Samuel Obenshain
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel, the oldest living settler in Whitley County, died near South Whitley, Indiana at his son's residence on May 24, 1869. He was born in Virginia but left that state over 50 years ago. He was one of the first settlers in the E
2 CONC el River Valley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel married Catharine Flora on 5 April 1819. She was born in Franklin County, Indiana. They lived in Virginia until 1835 when they moved to Ohio and in 1836 they moved to Cleveland Township in Whitley County, Indiana. Here he e
2 CONC ntered 160 acres of land in Section 11 and was one of the earliest settlers of the county.
