0 @I6000000114798144896@ INDI
1 NAME John /Obenchain/ Sr.
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Obenchain
2 NSFX Sr.
2 _MARNM Obenchain
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Jacksonville Cemetery 
2 ADDR
3 CITY Jacksonville
3 STAE Oregon
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 16 APR 1801
2 ADDR
3 STAE VA
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 AUG 1884
2 PLAC Jacksonville, Jackson, Oregon, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1838 John laid out the city of Fincastle, IN, located in the western part of Franklin Twp., Putnam Co., IN. John left IN in 1845 for IA and became a permanent settler in Buchanan Co. in 1846, building his shanty
2 CONC  2 miles north of Independence, IA, on what is now called "Obenchain's Creek". John was listed as being one of the early settlers of Washington Twp. Having built a rude shanty, he then commenced breaking prairie with ox and horse 
2 CONC teams, of which he had a large number and plenty of help; for he had a large family of grown boys. He obtained money to pay for his land by raising pork and then drawing it to Dubuque, a distance of 70 miles, and selling it for $2
2 CONC .25 per hundred. In the early years his house was ever open to the wanderer who had lost his way out on the pathless prairie. Many are still living in the county who can attest to the generous hospitality of the Virginian whose in
2 CONC tegrity and honesty were as true as the north star. He was also quite a hunter, always keeping a pack of hounds to track the deer, lynx, wildcat, and catamount. After he had remained in IA a few years, he built a fine, large log h
2 CONC ouse, and the same was used as a dwelling up to about 1880, when it accidentally caught fire and burned down; and there is now a large and commodious farm-house, that has been erected by the present owner. He remained in IA until 
2 CONC 1850 when he went overland to CA where he engaged in mining for gold. He returned to IA in 1853 and lived there until 1860; when, finding neighbors too many and near to be endured, he started for the wilds of OR. He settled finall
2 CONC y in Jackson Co., OR about 1862. John was in Oregon, with his cattle and savage bear dogs, his hair long and white; a patriarch as rough and rugged and intractable, and honest and sincere, as the mountains which surrounded him. [H
2 CONC istory of Buchanan County, Iowa, pp. 48, 202.] John was a Judge of Election in Township No. 1, Buchanan Co., IA in 1848. At first the townships were known simply by number. [History of Buchanan County, Iowa, p. 62.]
2 CONT
2 CONT John was in the 1870 & 1880 Census for Jackson Co., OR.
2 CONT
2 CONT History of Putnam Co., Indiana (Lewis Pub. Co., 1887), p. 221.
2 CONT History of Buchanan Co., Iowa (Williams Bros., 1881), pp. 42, 45, 48, 52, 62, 282.
2 CONT Census Records: 1830 Putnam Co,m IN, p. 217; 1840 Putnam Co., IN, p. 843; 1850 Buchanan Co., IA, p. 157.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was listed as age 48 in the 1850 Census of Buchanan Co., IA; occupation, farmer; birthplace, VA; Margaret was also listed as 48; birthplace, VA. The following children were listed: Mary Obenchain, age 24; Barkley Obenchain, a
2 CONC ge 23, farmer; Davis Obenchain, age 20, labourer; James Obenchain, age 18, labourer; George W. Obenchain, age 16, labourer; John Obenchain, age 8; & Madison Obenchain, age 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John Obenchain Memorial Photos Flowers Edit Share Learn about upgrading this memorial... Birth: 	1801 Death: 	1884
2 CONT
