1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Frederick Keister, II BIRTH	1730 Strasburg, Landkreis Vorpommern-Greifswald, Mecklenburg-Vorpommern, Germany DEATH	28 Nov 1815 (aged 84–85) Brandywine, Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA BURIAL	 Keister Cemetery 
2 CONC #3 • Plan a trip here Brandywine, Pendleton County, West Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/34966670/frederick-keister
2 CONT
2 CONT The DAR has him as Frederick Kiester.  DAR A 065662 , Virginia, Patriotic Service, Lt. ''''''Frederick Keister, Jr. was born in Strasbourgh, Germany, in 1730, son of Frederick Keister, Sr. (b.1704) & Hannah (________).
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Keister, Jr., came from Germany as a young boy on the ship "Virginia-Grace" on Sept. 24, 1737, and first settled in Lancaster & York Counties, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Keister, Jr. married Miss Hannah (Dyer) (1735-1820), daughter of Roger Dyer & Hannah (Smith), in Bath Co., Virginia, in 1755.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was an early pioneer settler on South Fork River near Brandywine, Augusta County  (now Pendleton County), (W.) Virginia, where his children were born and raised.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Keister, Jr. was naturalized on May 18, 1762 along with other German neighbors. (Abstracts of the Records of Augusta Co., Virginia, by Lyman Chalkley, Vol. 1, pg 97)
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick served in the Revolutionary War from Augusta & Rockingham Counties, Virginia, and qualified as Lieutenant in the Virginia Militia on Sept. 28, 1778.  (Virginia Militia in the Revolution, J. T. McAllister, pg. 230;  Abstr
2 CONC acts from the records of Augusta County, Virginia, Lyman Chalkley, Vol. II, pg. 364);  He was a member of a band of Indian scouts  and a 1st Lieutenant in the 46 th Regiment of the Virginia Militia in 1782;  He is also listed as f
2 CONC urnishing supplies in an account dated May 29, 1782  (A History of Rockingham County, Virginia, John W. Wayland, pg.101); & "Frederick Eister"  (List of Colonial Soldiers in Virginia, by H. J. Eckenrode, pg 37)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Frederick Keister" is listed on the 1792 Pendleton Co., (W.) Virginia, tax list
2 CONT
2 CONT "Fredericke Keister Sr"  (went by Sr. after his father died) is listed on the 1810 Pendleton County, (W.) Virginia, census as head of his household.    
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Keister's WILL was written in Pendleton County, (W.) Virginia, on August 10, 1806, and witnessed by John Davis, Robert Davis, Robert Davis, and Henry Puffenberger; It was proved on December 5, 1815.  He willed that "... 
2 CONC all my just debts and funeral charges be paid...to my dearly beloved wife one negro wench named Poll, two beds and beding, two pair bedsteds, one-third of all my moveable property...to my beloved sons, Frederick Keister and George
2 CONC  Keister, all my lands on this side of the river...to my son James Keister, all my lands on the side of the river he now lives on by paying 35 pounds...equally divided amongst all my daughters...appoint my wife, Hannah Keister, an
2 CONC d James Keister executors..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Keister, Jr., died in Pendleton Co., (W.) Virginia, on November 28, 1815, and he is buried in the Keister Cemetery #3 near Brandywine, Pendleton Co., W. Va., next to his wife.  Both his original headstone and a military 
2 CONC headstone added in 1931 are still present at his gravesite today. Inscription:
2 CONT
2 CONT NEWER HEADSTONE
2 CONT
2 CONT LT. FRED'K KEISTER ROCKINGHAM'S CO. REV. WAR 1730  1815
2 CONT
2 CONT OLD HEADSTONE
2 CONT
2 CONT   1815 F K x Nov 28
