1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elias went to Iowa with his Uncle Jacob in 1856, where he worked on a farm at ten dollars a month for 2 years.  Elias went to Schuyler Co., Illinois in 1858, where he worked for $14.00 a month. After his marriage i
2 CONC n 1860 Elias and his wife set up houskeeping on a farm owned by William W. Graham, 520 acres, In Section 2 in Birmingham Township, about 1892 they purchased 400 acres in Section 14, making 920 acres in all. Elias was a genial, soc
2 CONC iable and sympathtic gentleman.  He greatly benefited the township while he was serving as school director and road commision.
2 CONT
