1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/144945902/jonathan-hiser
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Jonathon Hiser BIRTH	30 Mar 1830 DEATH	18 Jan 1905 (aged 74) BURIAL	 Judy & Sites Cemetery Pansy, Grant County, West Virginia,
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/144945902/jonathon-hiser
2 CONT
2 CONT When the great Civil War began he espoused the cause of the Union, while his brothers sanctioned the South, two of them losing their lives in the great struggle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Hiser was born March 30, 1830 and died January 18th, 1905, and is survived by a brother and four sisters, and his wife and fourteen children.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Ellen Judy in 1855, and after her death he married Mary J. Landes in 1872. The first union was blessed with seven children, two only surviving him, and the last by twelve, all of whom are living.
2 CONT
2 CONT All the children except Mrs. Landes were present at the cemetery to witness the last sad rites.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born and raised in Pendleton County, and spent about fifty years of his life in his native county. He was of German descent, and was a typical American gentleman, kind hearted, jovial, sympathetic and witty, always having k
2 CONC ind words for the young.
2 CONT
2 CONT When a young man, being a gifted singer, it was his heart's delight after working hard all week on his father's farm to walk five or six miles to teach a class in music.
