1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Delilah Conrad Hammer BIRTH	1 Sep 1813 Ruddle, Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA DEATH	30 Aug 1904 (aged 90) Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA BURIAL	 Ruddle Presbyterian Church Cemetery Pendleton County, Wes
2 CONC t Virginia, USA  MEMORIAL ID	106760172
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/106760172
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary; On Tuesday morning of August 30, our hearts were made sad when it was announced that Mrs. Delilah Hammer was dead. (Better known as Aunt Delilah)
2 CONT
2 CONT For nearly 91 years this good woman lived among us, and even the stranger seemed to know her, and the beggar as well, for neither ever went hungry from her door.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her maiden name was Conrad, she was born September the 1st, 1813, near her late home at Ruddle. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 7th 1831, she was married to Elias Hammer, to this union were born 16 children, 8 girls and 8 boys.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a woman of extraordinary strength both of body and mind, and until the last 2 or 3 years she was able to work and manage her household affairs.
2 CONT
2 CONT He husband died about 36 years ago, some of her children died when quite small, and some were taken in manhood and womanhood. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Many of the soldiers of the Civil War remember her more as a mother than a friend for many times were they fed by her kind hand and many times she gave them the alarm of danger, sometimes in the cold dark night, and we can say the
2 CONC re is but few who have borne as great trials and troubles of this world, as this good woman did, yet she was brave and never shrank from duty of any kind, seldom was she known to murmur, she trusted to God, who doeth all things, a
2 CONC nd would say Gods ways are not ours and we must submit to his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT About 20 years ago she united with the Presbyterian church, and lived a true Christian to the time of her death.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Wednesday the 31st her remains were laid to rest on the New Cemetery near the Ruddle church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT {Abstracted from Pendleton County Obituaries}
2 CONT
2 CONT Contributed by: Shock
