1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Photo added by Karl R. Kiser to Find A Grave memorial.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Taylor Hammer BIRTH	13 Sep 1847 Virginia, USA DEATH	17 Jul 1907 (aged 59) Ruddle, Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA BURIAL	 Ruddle Presbyterian Church Cemetery Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA  MEMORIAL ID	106760186
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/106760186
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary: Died at his home in Ruddle, W.Va., on July 17, Mr. I.T. Hammer, the deceased was born near the place of his death, September 13, 1847 and was the son of Elias and Delilah Hammer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was united in marriage December 7, 1878 with Miss. Fannie Conrad, the only daughter of Laban and Rachel Conrad.
2 CONT
2 CONT A few years later they begin housekeeping on a small farm with no improvements.
2 CONT
2 CONT To this union were born 7 children, 2 daughters and 5 sons. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They worked both early and late, practiced economy, were honest and upright in all things and prospered, as their pennies accumulated they did not forget that God was the giver of all things and they gave freely of what they posse
2 CONC ssed to the church, the poor and the heathen and beautified their home.
2 CONT
2 CONT This home was one in which the neighbor, the visitor, the beggar and the stranger were always welcome, none ever left their door hungry or unaided in time of need.
2 CONT
2 CONT The traveling men, the ministers and many others who have gone from that home will ever cherish his memory for his hospitality.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a man whose influence will live on, a man whose life is worthy of imitation and was a man of high christian character.
2 CONT
2 CONT His unflinching obedience to all the calls of honor and duty belonging to the home, the church and the public.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was always ready to defend the right and conquer his enemies with love and kindness, he was a safe counselor for all who came to him for advice.
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived a consistent christian life and was always found in his place at church, especially in Sunday School work. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He had been Superintendent of our Sunday School for at least 20 years and was a ruling Elder in the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT No man stood higher in this community among those who knew him than Mr. Hammer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had the esteem and high regard of every one and no person could speak of him but in praise.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was of quiet disposition and reserved but of strong convictions of right and lived up to his profession.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was an affectionate and indulgent father, a true and devoted husband and came as near living up to the golden rule as any man could come. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral took place at noon on Thursday the 18th in the Presbyterian church of which he was a member, it being one of the largest ever held here, the sermon was preached by his pastor Rev. S.S. Oliver, after which his remains w
2 CONC ere laid to rest in the cemetery overlooking his home.
2 CONT
2 CONT {Abstracted from Pendleton County Obituaries}
2 CONT
2 CONT Contributed by: Shock
