1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mr. Hammer when a mere boy of about sixteen, volunteered his services to the cause of the South in the Civil War, and was brave and courageous in his service to his country just as he has ever since been to his gov
2 CONC ernment and state. He was a member of the famous 62nd Virginia Regiment, Company F, under General Imboden, the glory and renown of which regiment will be recounted as long as history lasts. He was staunch Democrat and always took 
2 CONC a keen interest in his party and the welfare of his county and the State.
