1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/140240437
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Hammer was one of a family of fourteen children and was the son of George and Mary Harper Hammer, who both lived to a good age and who were very highly respected citizens of this county.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of this family who survive are Mrs. Phebe Ann Hammer, Mrs David Mallow, Mrs. Chas A. Hedrick, George W. Hammer and Benj. S. Hammer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Clay Hammer left this county when about twenty years of age and settled in Dayton, Ohio, where he was for many years engaged as expert cabinet maker, with the Cash Register Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Miss Margaret Snyder and they lived a long a happy life together. To this union two sons, Clyde and Karel Hammer, were born. They with their mother survive him.
2 CONT
