1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary Catherine Byrd Trumbo
2 CONT BIRTH
2 CONT 11 Feb 1854
2 CONT Franklin, Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA
2 CONT DEATH
2 CONT 20 Feb 1934 (aged 80)
2 CONT Brandywine, Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT Pine Hill Cemetery
2 CONT Brandywine, Pendleton County, West Virginia,
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/5757438/mary-catherine-trumbo
2 CONT
2 CONT Newspaper Obiturary
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mary C. Trumbo
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mary Catherine Trumbo departed this life early Tuesday morning, February 20, 1934, at the advanced age of 80 years and 9 days.  Her death came as quite a shock as she was apparently in the best of health.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a daughter of the late James W. and Mary Ann Byrd and was the last surviving member of her family.  Her brothers, John W. Byrd and Clay O. Byrd, and her sister Mrs. Adelaide Davis all died shortly before reaching the age o
2 CONC f fifty years.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was united in marriage with Morgan G. Trumbo November 13, 1879 and their marriage ceremony was performed by the Rev. John A. Preston of the Presbyterian Church.  To this union six children were born, five of which survive.
2 CONT
2 CONT The oldest son, Aude Byrd Trumbo who died October 18, 1902, at the age of 21 years, at Welch, W. Va., was just graduated from the Dunsmore Business School at Staunton, Va., and had accepted a position as bookkeeper when he was str
2 CONC icken and died of typhoid fever.
2 CONT
2 CONT The death of her husband,M. G. Trumbo, occurred August 1, 1904, at Charleston, W. Va., while he was a member of the West Virginia Legislature.
2 CONT
2 CONT The five surviving children are, Dr. G. C. Trumbo, of Norfolk, Va.;  L. D. Trumbo, a merchant of Brandywine;  Mrs. Harry Kiser, of Greely, Colorado;  Mrs. Walter G. Simpson and Miss Cleda Trumbo, of Brandywine.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are also seven granddaughters and two grandsons surviving.
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased was a faithful member of the Christian Church for many years and through her work on this earth is finished and her voice is still, the influence of her christian life will live on forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Thursday morning at the Chritian Church at Brandywine, by Rev. J. O. Patterson, former pastor of the Brandywine church, now of Paw Paw, W. Va.-- one who knew her and loved her.
