3 STAE West Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 28 JAN 1856
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 MAY 1905
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John W. Byrd Dead
2 CONT
2 CONT  The town and the neighborhood were much awe stricken when the physicians made it known that Jon. W. Byrd, was in a dangerous condition, with but little hopes for his recovery.
2 CONT
2 CONT  For a number of hours he lay in an unconscious state and as the day was closing Monday life became extinct and the soul took its flight to the God, who gave it.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Mr. Byrd is truly a loss to the entire county.
2 CONT
2 CONT  In an official capacity the county has never had a better and safer man.
2 CONT
2 CONT  As a teacher in the public schools he did what duty demanded.
2 CONT
2 CONT  When he was sheriff of the county the office was never left in better condition.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He served as a member of the county court and likewise made a record.
2 CONT
2 CONT  In politics Mr. Byrd was clean handed and elevated himself above usual politics.
2 CONT
2 CONT  The neighborhood recognized in him an exemplary character.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Mr. Byrd became a member of the Presbyterian church during the pastorate of Rev. J. Spencer Smith, and has since led a Christian life.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was preceded to the grave by his wife seven or more years ago. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving him are two sons, Don and Ernest and a daughter Mrs. Gordon Boggs.
2 CONT
2 CONT  [obit torn here]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks, Karl Kiser, for the obit & adding pics
