1 DEAT
2 DATE 26 DEC 1906
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mrs. Adelaide Davis, wife of ex-Sheriff Geo. W. Davis, formally of this county, but now of Elkins, W. Va., died at her home this morning of typhoid fever, after an illness lasting but little over two weeks.
2 CONT
2 CONT  From the beginning of her illness Mrs. Davis insisted that she would not get well, but her friends hoped that she might be mistaken.
2 CONT
2 CONT  On Saturday her condition seemed to her physician so favorable that her only son, Ona E. Davis left home for a visit to Franklin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Scarcely had he arrived in the county when he received a message from his father that if he wished to see his mother alive he would have to come at once.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was unable to reach home before news of her death arrived. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased was a daughter of the late James Byrd. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a woman of more than ordinary intelligence and strength of character, and had many friends here.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Interment will take place Friday in the Byrd burying-ground, 3 miles north of Franklin.
2 CONT
2 CONT  The deceased is survived by her husband Geo. W. Davis; her only son, Ona E. Davis; and a sister, Mrs. M.G. Trumbo of Brandywine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Franklin, W.Va., - December 26, 1906
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks Karl Kiser for obit & pics.
