1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A207590  DAR Ancestor #: A207590]
2 CONT
2 CONT PETER NEIGHSWONGER
2 CONT
2 CONT was born in 1755 near Winchester, Frederick County, VA. He and his brothers, Jacob and John, moved to the Wheeling, presently WV, area in 1773.
2 CONT
2 CONT They were Rangers in the Virginia militia under Capt. Peter Helphenstine. Jacob died in 1775. John was killed by Indians in 1783 on a hunting expedition down the Ohio river, near Little Grave creek. His partner, Joseph Heffler, es
2 CONC caped as their canoe floated off down river. John was found some months later near Captiva island still in his canoe. Hamilton Kerr, Peter's brother-in-law, eventually killed the Indian that killed John.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter then served under Lt. David Enoch. Peter was married to Jane Kerr and their son, Hamilton, was born in 1784 (Probably named after his uncle). Peter was a hunter and defender of the settlement at Wheeling and Fort Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT from: http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSsr=361&GSvcid=88304&GRid=76870096&
