1 NAME Abner /Cooper/
2 GIVN Abner
2 _MARNM Cooper
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 27 MAR 1763
2 PLAC Middletown, Middlesex County, Connecticut, British Colonial America (CT US)
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1 JAN 1837
2 ADDR
3 CITY Springfield
3 STAE PA
3 POST 16914
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Age 73 years, 9 months, 5 days
2 CONT
2 CONT Served in Rev. War between 1779 and 1781. [Source: Record of Service of Connecticut Men, Part I, Connecticut Militia, 1775-1783, p. 582.] Abner was a scout for the Americans. Abner and his cousin Hagier were nephews of William Coo
2 CONC per, father of Laban. Pension record indicates Abner was a pvt. for 2 mos. in 1779 under Capt. Wells; 2 mos. in 1780 under Capt. Norris and Col. Willis; and 3 mos. in 1781 under Capt. Starr (sp?) and Col. Canfield, all in CT. Bega
2 CONC n receiving a pension on 4 March 1831 of $23.33 per year. [Source: Connecticut Officers and Soldiers, 1700s-1800s, Connecticut Revolutionary Pensions, p. 44.]
2 CONT Between 1800 and 1819 he lived in Elmira, NY. After 1819 he lived in Bentley Creek, PA (farm owned by Arthur McClelland in 1964). He was buried in small family cemetery south of Beulah Thompson's home in southern Bentley Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Descendants of Wilhelm Abendschon (Ovenshire)
