1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Death of Frank Ovenshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Frank Ovenshire, an old and highly respected citizen, died at his home, known as the Ovenshire place, on Saturday night last. He was sixty-nine years old March 29th. His sufferings were at times of the most intense nature duri
2 CONC ng his sickness, it having been about four months since he had taken to his bed. He has been a resident of this valley for many years, and of late was in the employ of the Lehigh Valley company, keeping accounts of stock in the su
2 CONC pply house.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a native of this county, having been born just across the river. He was highly respected and honored by all, generous and kind-hearted. The possessor of a quiet and friendly way, he always made himself agreeable to stranger
2 CONC s who were so fortunate as to make his acquaintance. He leaves a wife and daughter to mourn his departure, who are consoled on every side by sympathizing friends. The funeral obsequies took place from his former residence Wednesda
2 CONC y morning and were largely attended.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Newspapers.com
