2 CONT <br/>Enlisted on July 12, 1863 (Mustered in September 14, 1863 - Mustered out with regiment August 20, 1865). Regimental Officer was Col. John E. Phelps
2 CONT
2 CONT Old stone has birth date of June 15, 1827 - PVT CO F 2 ARK CAV Civil War of the Fed States Army (2 Military Markers)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elias Auvenshine - Private - Co. "F" Enlisted July 12, 1863 - Mustered in September 14, 1863 - Mustered out with regiment August 20, 1865. Regimental Officer was Col. John E. Phelps
2 CONT
2 CONT Elias Auvenshine AKA William Elias Auvenshine, served with Co F 2 Regiment Arkansas Cavalry. He was 36 years old, Height; 5 feet 8 inches, Complexion; Fair, Eyes; Blue, Hair; light. Where born; Warren County, Tennessee, Occupation
2 CONC ; Farmer. Enlistment July 12, 1863 in Springfield, Missouri, by James L. Powell for a term of 3 years. On the Muster Roll for January and February 1864, in the remarks it states, "Absent without leave since 24 Feb 64 in Polk Co., 
2 CONC Mo." On the Muster roll for March and April he is listed as present and in the remarks is stated "Bounty unpaid," which shows he returned voluntarily. On the Muster Roll for September and October 1864 in the Remarks, "Detached ser
2 CONC vice to North Mo. since 27 Sept 1864."
