2 CONT * William Propst 
2 CONT * Born February 17, 1831 [location unknown]
2 CONT * Son of Henry Propst JR and Mary Catherine Cress
2 CONT * Brother of Elizabeth Propst, Eleanor Propst, Louisa Catherine Propst, Rebecca Propst and Eli Alexander Propst	
2 CONT * Husband of Henrietta Caroline Ritchie — married [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT * Father of Mary Lucretia Propst, Alice E. Propst, John William Propst Sr and Henry L. Propst	
2 CONT * Died August 11, 1919 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.gorowan.com/rowanroots/family_files/propst.html 3. CAPT. WILLIAM3 PROPST (HENRY PROPST2 JR., HENRY (HEINRICH) PROPST1 SR.) was born 17 Feb 1831, and died 11 Aug 1919 in Cabarrus County, NC. He married HENRITTA CAROLINA 
2 CONC RITCHIE 02 Jun 1855, daughter of JOHN RITCHIE and CELIA BLACKWELDER. She was born 01 Oct 1834, and died 03 Aug 1920.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for CAPT. WILLIAM PROPST:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd. Lt. William Propst served in the Civil War. He enlisted on 7th. July, 1862 in Cabarrus County in Company "F" 57th. NCST. He enlisted when Company F organized in Concord in July 1862. Propst was captured at the Battle of Chanc
2 CONC ellorsville, May 4, 1863, but was exchanged in time to rejoin his regiment for the Gettysburg campaign. He was shot in the side at Gettysburg and was one of the thousands of wounded Confederates abandoned when the Army of Northern
2 CONC  Virginia retreated at the conclusion of the battle. He was imprisioned until exchanged on May 8, 1864. He returned to duty, and was recaptured again at the Battle of Hatcher's Run, Virginia, on February 6, 1865. He was imprisoned
2 CONC  at Old Capitol Prison, Washington, DC., & Fort Delaware, DE. He was released on June 8, 1865, after taking the Oath of Allegiance.
