1 NOTE {geni:about_me} George Franklin Obenchain, son of Samuel Obenchain and Catharine Flora Obenchain was born May 1, 1826 in Franklin County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1835, George moved with his parents to Ohio from Virginia when he was nine years old. In 1836, he moved again with the family to Whitley Co. Indiana where his father purchased 160 acres of land. At age twenty-three, he was unit
2 CONC ed in marriage to Arrena Flecher. George and Arrena had three children together, Alfred, Mary and James Melvin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrena died in 1876 and is buried in Centerville Cemetery in Indiana. It should be noted that George's farm is adjacent to this cemetery. At one time he owned his own 82 acre farm, but the government acquired this land along with 
2 CONC about 3,000 acres for airfield during WW2.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Arrena, George married Sarah Ellen Rothrock in 1877. There was nearly a twenty-eight year difference in their ages. To this union, four children were born.
2 CONT
2 CONT George is buried by Arrena in Lawrence Co., Illinois. George and Arrena were members of the Church of the Brethren.
