1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Catherine Propst Mucklewain BIRTH	16 Mar 1772 USA DEATH	14 Aug 1849 (aged 77) Calhoun County, West Virginia, USA BURIAL	 Winner Cemetery Calhoun County, West Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/43691982/catherine-mucklewain
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Photo George Frederick McElwain 1794–1854
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo Nancy Mucklewain Starcher 1816–1871
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Catherine Propst
2 CONT *BIRTH	16 Mar 1772 USA
2 CONT *DEATH	14 Aug 1849 (aged 77) Calhoun County, West Virginia, USA
2 CONT *BURIAL	Winner Cemetery Calhoun County, West Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ..... 3 TUNIS ANTHONY "McELWAIN" WAYNE b: August 19, 1759 in VA d: November 4, 1851 in Calhoun Co., VA (WV)
2 CONT
2 CONT ......... +CATHERINE PROPST b: March 15, 1772 m: 1789 in Pendleton Co., VA d: August 4, 1849 in Calhoun Co., VA (WV)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://hackerscreek.com/norman/PROBST.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine Elizabeth Propst, a daughter of George Frederick and Barbara (Swadley/Pence) Propst, was born March 15, 1772 and died August 4, 1849 in Calhoun County, VA (WV). She reportedly married James McQuain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Tunis Anthony McElwain in Pendleton County VA in 1791. Tunis was a son of George and Nancy (Rector) McElwain. His monument in the Ball-Winter cemetery in Calhoun County WV gives a birth date of August 19, 1773 and deat
2 CONC h date of November 4, 1851. However, his American Revolution Veteran's pension file contains a December 10, 1833 deposition stating that he was 74 years on the date of the deposition. A Virginia Militia record states that he was 7
2 CONC 5 years old March 4, 1831. Since his claim for a Revolutionary War service pension was validated, he was probably born about 1760.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1797, the family moved from Pendleton County to Franklin County, VA and lived there until 1802, when they returned to Pendleton,County, where they remained until 1812.  In 1812 they moved to the,banks of the Elk River and settl
2 CONC ed at the mouth of the Holly River.mTunis had 54 acres surveyed October 18, 1815 and received a land grant
2 CONT from the Commonwealth of Virginia December 30, 1816. In 1830, themfamily moved to the West Fork of the Little Kanawha River in Kanawha,County, VA near the present site of Arnoldsburg, Calhoun County, WV. The 1850 Gilmer County cen
2 CONC sus lists Tunis in the household of his son in law, Soloman Nicholas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tunis Anthony and Catherine (Propst) McElwain are buried in the Ball-Winter Cemetary, near Arnoldsburg, Calhoun County, WV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links 
2 CONT * http://lionstime.com/waynemcelwain.html
