2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Smith was BORN in Cecil Co., Maryland, in c1704, a DAUGHTER of William Smith II (born England c1650, died Cecil Co, MD 1708); and GRAND-DAUGHTER of William Smith I (died 1710 Cecil Co., MD) & Grace (Jermin) who immigrated f
2 CONC rom England to Cecil Co., Maryland
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger Dyer was born about 1700 and was killed in Augusta County VA at the Ft. Seybert Indian massacre in 1758.  He married Hannah Smith. Hannah was born about 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Roger and Hannah (Smith) Dyer.
2 CONT
2 CONT *  2.  (1). William                                 d.Apr 28 1758         m.Margaret Hiett 
2 CONT *  3.  (2). Hester                  b.c.     1731   d.       1820         m.Matthew Patton 
2 CONT *  5.  (3). Sarah                                   d.       1818         m.Henry Hawes 
2 CONT * 6.  (4). Hannah                  b.c.     1735        m.Frederick Keister
2 CONT *  7.  (5). James                   b.c.     1744   d.       1807         m.Phoebe Ann Harrison
2 CONT
2 CONT —-
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of birth have also been (erroneously?) reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * circa 1699 at an unspecified location
2 CONT * 1705 in Pennsylvania
