2 CONT "Lair" Dean married Mahala Crites Dean on March 19, 1835 in Lewis County, (West)Virginia. They were the parents to about 16 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is a transcription of the obituary for Lair Dean. The newspaper was not readable in some areas.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Buckhannon Delta, Buckhannon, West Virginia. May 16, 1891 (Microfilm copy)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''Obituary:'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT At his home in Braxton county, West Virginia, Lair Dean a prominent member and local preacher of the M. E. Church departed this life May 11th, 1891 in the 81st year of his life. He leaves in this cold world, an aged companion; nin
2 CONC e sons, one daughter and many relatives, to mourn his departure,  Father  Dean   was much respected as a good citizen and  Christian  gentleman by all who knew him, and in his death a kind  father,  affectionate  husband and faith
2 CONC ful follower of Christ and will be missed.  Much of his time for a number of years was spent in the work of the Lord and  we feel sure that many can attribute their return to God, through his hallo//////// influence in Christ, Whi
2 CONC l////////////////tender/// tie /////////////////// (not legible) ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////// their  hearts,  yet  are  they  confident-dent  that  a  husband  and  father has  
2 CONC gone to  that  land where  God shall wipe away  all  tears   from their eyes, and  there shall be  no more death neither sorrow nor crying, for in Heaven they ever bloom in the vigor of an immortal youth. On  the afternoon of the 
2 CONC 15th after a short funeral service, in the presence of a number of people we quietly laid to rest in the Morrison church yard cemetery the body of Father Dean, Blessed is he whose life is bid with Christ in God .             OLIVE
2 CONC R WESTFALL    (  //// - can not read this area on microfilm of paper.)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinad Lair Dean  (s/o John Dean 1750-1813 and Mary Knicely  1764-1855)  and Mahala  (d/o Leonard Crites) 1789-1869 and Mary Bozarth Forinash 1789-1817), 
2 CONT Children: James, Mary, Lucinda , Elizabeth, William, David, Jacob W., Jno W., Isaac N., Harrison L , Marshall F., Harrison L., Leonard A., Marsha F. and Abraham P. - DEAN.
2 CONT
