2 CONT OBITUARY- W.B. Dean Died In Maryland Hospital
2 CONT
2 CONT Wateman (sp.Waitman) Bernard Dean, 82, whose home was on the Kesling Mill Road, died on Friday night at 7 o'clock at the Garrett Memorial Hospital at Oakland, Md.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born Sept.7, 1886 in Upshur County, a son of the late George and Lucinda Hinkle Dean. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On Nov.1, 1908 he married Audree Queen, who survives. Also surviving are one son Bernard Dean, supervisor of pupil personnel in Garrett County Schools, whose home is at Accident, Md., and a daughter Mrs. Virginia Carr of Route 5; 
2 CONC and 4 grandchildren and 7 great grandchildren. He was the last of a family of 11.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the Kesling United Methodist Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held at the Whitescarver-Rundio Funeral Home Monday afternoon at 2 o'clock with the Rev. Owen Lee, of Morgantown, officiating. Burial was made in the Buckhannon Memorial Park
