1 NOTE {geni:about_me} George was killed during the massacre at FortSeybert on 4-28-1758. It appears that 7 year old Elizabeth wasone of the children taken captive by the Shawnee ChieftainKillbuck. Elizabeth next appears 7 years later wh
2 CONC en on 5-21-1765an Augusta County VA Court approved her choice of John Dunkle asher guardian. This John Dunkle was a neighbor of NicholasHevener and of Frederick, his son and Elizabeth's futurehusband, in the South Branch community
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT George Mouse was born about 1715 and emigrated in 1740. Itappears that he spent but little time in Pennsylvania as his isrecorded in the Pendleton County records of 1749 with reguard toan appraisal of property he owned on the Sout
2 CONC h Branch. There wasalso a Frederick Mouse noted in the Augusta County records of1760 as being a brother and next of kin to the senior GeorgeMouse, deceased.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT George Mauss BIRTH	1715 Germany DEATH	28 Apr 1758 (aged 42–43) Fort Seybert, Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA BURIAL	 Fort Seybert Massacre Gravesite Pendleton County, West Virginia,
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/43978522/george-mauss
2 CONT
2 CONT George was killed after the fort was given over the Killbuck and his men. George's daughter Elizabeth was taken by Killbuck and his men.
