1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA with the rank of PRIVATE.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A104495  DAR Ancestor # A104495]
2 CONT
2 CONT Revolutionary War Soldier - Private of Virginia Emigrated in 1773 Landing in Dumfries, Va "According to Ritchie County History, by Minnie Kendall Lowther, "He had been one of the King's waiters for 7 years before coming to America
2 CONC . Finding such service distastefulhe one day wandered down to the harbor just as a vessel eas ready to set sail for the Colonies. Without further deliberation, he stepped on board and turned his face toward the west. When he lande
2 CONC d on these shores, he found himself penniless in a land of strangers, and was sold for his fare to Jacob Conrad, whom he served for four years to cancel the debt. He served as an soldier in Lord dunmore's War, being under the dire
2 CONC ct command of Genreal Lewis as the Battle of Point Pleasant, and he also served as an American Soldier in the Revolutionary War. Patrick Sinnett married Catharine Hevener (Heffner) on May 1 1783 in Pendleton Co, VA --Walter L Eye 
2 CONC book pg 1"  Indentured to Jacob Conrad when he landed in Dumfries VA http://followingtheirfootsteps.net/getperson.php?personID=I6413&tree=Owings
2 CONT --------------------
