1 NOTE {geni:about_me} M  George Edward HISERPrint Family Tree Born 17 August 1875 - Grant, West Virginia Deceased 9 October 1944 - Ridgeley, Allegany, West Virginia , age at death: 69 years old
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to Sarah Susan IMAN
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to Mary BARR 1891-1982
2 CONT
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/jjmorehead?lang=en&p=george+edward&n=hiser
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary: "George Edward Hiser, 69, a Ridgeley grocer, dropped dead at 8:45 this morning as the result of a heart attack. He was carrying a glass of water when stricken and sustained cuts about the face in the fall. Mr. Hiser fell
2 CONC  to the ground in front of his place of business, corner of Blocker and Lyons street, while returning from an apartment above the store where he had gone to get a glass of water with which to take a dose of medicine. He complained
2 CONC  about not feeling well. A doctor was summoned and reported Mr. Hiser had died instantly. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Hiser was a native of West Virginia and a son of the late Jonathan and Mary (Landis) Hiser. He is survived by the widow, Mrs. Mary (Barr) Hiser, and three daughters, Mrs. Joseph Weaver and Mrs. T. W. Smith, both of St. Petersb
2 CONC urg, Fla., and Mrs. John Morrow, Hadden Heights, N. J. Three brothers, William and B. P. Hiser of Petersburg, W. Va., and Jesse Hiser, of Baltimore; four sisters, Mrs. Rita Duncan, Deer Run, W.Va., Mrs. Grace Boor, of Cumberland, 
2 CONC Mrs. Viola Ritchie, of Petersburg, W. Va., and Mrs. Robert Shockey, of Keyser, and one grandson, James Morrow, also survive. The body has been taken to the home and funeral services will be held Wednesday afternoon at two o'clock 
2 CONC at the Ridgeley Methodist church with the Rev. E. G. A. Snider and the Rev. R. L. Greynolds, officiating. Burial will be in the Fort Ashby cemetery." -Published in The Cumberland Evening Times, Monday, October 9, 1944
