1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=77548327 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Feb. 9, 1817 Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Apr. 29, 1898 Grant County West Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Abijah Dolly was born in Hardy Co., Virginia (now Grant Co., West Virginia). He served as a justice of the Hardy County Court at the beginning of the Civil War and worked to include the county in the new state of West Virginia. He
2 CONC  was a member of the West Virginia constituional convention and served as Hardy County's representative in the new state's House of Delgates.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a member of the local federal home guard, Dolly captured an English adventurer on a spy mission for Dixie in 1863 on his farm in what is now Grant Co., West Virginia. The Englishman was an author and included the episode in his
2 CONC  book BORDER AND BASTILLE.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abijah Dolly married first to Jemima Michael in 1838. She bore him nine children before her death in 1871. Three years later he married again to Ruhama George and there were eight more children. Abijah Dolly died in 1898 near Mart
2 CONC in, West Virginia. (Bio by Mark Hale, citing THE HERO OF GREENLAND GAP)
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
