1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography==
2 CONT A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA with the rank of LIEUTENANT
2 CONT
2 CONT Lieutenant in the Revolutionary War, Yohogania County Militia. Will dated 14 Feb 1818, proved 18 Dec 1820.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1780, David and his family, accompanied by brothers Colonel Isaac Cox II, Benjamin Cox, and Joseph Cox, and several other families including William Chanoweth, Colonel James Rogers with three brothers Matthew Rogers, Jonathan R
2 CONC ogers and William Bard Rogers (Bardstown, KY named after him) - and perhaps Jacob Decker and James McDonald moved from Virginia (West Virginia) by flatboats down the Ohio River to the "Falls of the Ohio" and then to Cox's Creek an
2 CONC d established Cox's Station about five miles northeast of Bardstown, KY, today. (Ancestry Message Board by Scott McMahon, 1998)
2 CONT
2 CONT His parents were Isaac Cox, I, and Susannah Tomlinson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
