1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/30884410/george-cox
2 CONT
2 CONT A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A027004  DAR Ancestor #  A027004]
2 CONT
2 CONT George was born in Hampshire County Virginia in 1749. He settled on the Ohio River in what is now Brooke County in about 1772. He married Susanna Decker in 1775 and their known children were Isaac, Joseph, James, George, Friend, J
2 CONC onantha, Nancy and Susannah.
2 CONT
2 CONT      He and his family lived in what is now Wellsburg and he died December 1835. His will was filed in Brooke County on 25, December 1837.
2 CONT
2 CONT      He served his country proudly in both the Revolutionary War and Lord Dunsmore' s War. He enlisted the spring of 1775 with his brother's company, Captain Isaac Cox and Lt. Steel of the 14th Virginia Line. He was placed on the 
2 CONC pension rolls, but was dropped like many others of this area, in 1835 since his unit was to protect their homes from Indians and not a regularly constituted military unit.
2 CONT
2 CONT      While no marker of his actual burial spot has been found it has been documented that his body was moved from the Old Cox burial ground to this cemetery. This seems to be quite possible as so many other of his family and frien
2 CONC ds are buried here. 
2 CONT
2 CONT from: http://www.brookecountywvgenealogy.org/revwar.html
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Added from Family Tree compiled by Priscilla Buchanan [given to me 3/21/2012]
