1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/103291070/nancy_ann-worrell
2 CONT The following information from Marla Weaver Find A Grave #48071077 on 3 Jul 2018:
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorial 103291070 - Nancy Ann Cox Wellsburg
2 CONT Hi, I am a direct descendant of Nancy "Ann" Cox McMahon. I am having difficulty in why her name was changed to "Wellsburg?" She was first married to William McMahon and then she married Edward Worrell in Brooke Co., Va now WV. Her
2 CONC  name should be Nancy "Ann" Cox McMahon Worrell. She died in Wellsburg, WV so that is maybe why there is confusion. I have numerous Brook Co., WV deeds where Ann was left land by her 1st husband William McMahon was sold by her and
2 CONC  her 2nd husband Edward Worrell. There is no mistaking that this land was owned by William McMahon because he was mentioned as her deceased husband and some deeds mentioned the children of William. I do not know where Ann is burie
2 CONC d but probably someplace in Brooke Co. I know her 2nd husband, Ed Worrell, was still alive in 1835 because he sold land to a Danforth Brown and this land had previously been his wife's land that passed to her when 1st husband Will
2 CONC iam McMahon died. I have a lot of info on both the Cox's and McMahon's since I belong to the DAR through both patriot names. Sincerely, Marla
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy Ann Cox McMahon Wellsburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Isaac Cox & Susannah Tomlinson.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following information from Sue McDuffie FAG #47122067:
2 CONT
2 CONT I have found several sources that indicate Nancy first married William McMahon 21 Mar 1774 in Hampshire Co, VA or WV.  She secondly married Edward Worrel Wellsburg 15 Oct 1797 in Brooke Co, WV.  She died there on 17 Jan 1818 in We
2 CONC llsburg, Brooke County, WV.  No memorial for Edward.  They did not have children.  Also, I have not located a cemetery for Nancy. Please change her death location, and her last name to Wellsburg.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/103291070/nancy_ann-worrell Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 1 2025, 16:42:01 UTC''
2 CONT ----
