1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Michael Bechtel Ludwig was born 14 February 1745 in Amity Township, Berks Co. Pa. He was the son of Hans Michael Ludwig and Eva Rosina (Bechtel) Ludwig. He married Maria Susanna Lutz 25 December 1768 in Philadelphi
2 CONC a, Philadephia Co , Pa.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Revolutionary War, Michael was a member of John Sands Company of Pennsylvania Militia.He hauled supplies to Washington's Army at Valley Forge. DAR Ancestor #: A072346
2 CONT
2 CONT As one of the representative citizens of Amity Township, Michael was instrumental in the building of the Church at Amityville. He was a farmer by trade. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died 15 March 1806 in Amity Township, Berks Co. Pa. He was buried 17 March 1806 in Amityville Lutheran Church Cemetery in Amityville.Michael and his wife , Susanna Lutz (1751-1818) Ludwig are buried in the churchyard on the eas
2 CONC tside near the Church. Their graves are marked with large flat marble slabs.
