1 TITL Lt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Husband of Mary Sinclair
2 CONT
2 CONT US Civil War; 2nd LT Co H 8th Regt Pa Vol
2 CONT
2 CONT Pennsylvania Veterans Burial Cards, 1777-1999
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT THE POST-STANDARD, 8YRACU8E, N. Y., SUNDAY MORNING, DECEMBER 30, 1917
2 CONT
2 CONT SERVICE IS ARRANGED FOR WILLIAM D SNYDER
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral of Civil War Veteran to be Held at Onondaga Valley
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral of William D Snyder, 79, a veteran of the Civil War will be held at 2:30 o'clock tomorrow afternoon at his home in Onondaga Valley. The body will be taken to Scranton, PA for burial Tuesday morning by Cornell, Clement 
2 CONC & Wright, undertakers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Snyder died Friday night.  He was born in Scranton and organized the first company to leave that city in 1861, serving as the second lieutenant.  About eleven years ago he moved to Onondaga Valley, where he became a member of t
2 CONC he M E Church.  Surviving are his widow, Mrs Mary Snyder; two sons, Charles S Snyder of Syracuse and Harry R Snyder of Milwaukee, Wis. and one sister, Mrs J B Floyd, of Waverly.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/694
2 CONC 29292/william-daniel-snyder Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 27 2023, 4:09:42 UTC''
2 CONT
