1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://books.google.com/books?id=o4dHPdGT9nwC&lpg=PA1973&ots=mLIT4dSOEI&pg=PA1973#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter, son of Samuel and Sibylla Filbert, was born at Bernville, Berks county, in 1794.  His father died when he was about six months old,leaving his two sons to the guardianship of their grandfathers, Phillip Filbert and Francis 
2 CONC Umbenhaur.  In 1814 he enlisted with the troops called out for the defense of Baltimore against the British army, and marched under Captain Smith to Springfield camp, near that city, and after the retreat of the British was honora
2 CONC bly discharged from service.  He married Elizabeth, daughter of John Stoudt, in 1818, and the next year removed to Pine Grove, Schuykill county, PA, to take charge of the Pine Grove Forge.  Mr. Filbert was the presidential elector
2 CONC  chosen to represent this district in the election of 1840, and cast his vote for the successful candidate, William Henry Harrison.  he died February 14, 1864.
