1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Revolutionary War..... New York  Continental troops  private
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT lived in Tulpehocken.
2 CONT
2 CONT See more info at Morton Montgomery's 1909 log of Berks families: http://berks.pa-roots.com/books/montgomery/k10.html#LeviAKilmer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Information from http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=65141476:  
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Nov. 23, 1736 Philadelphia Philadelphia County Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Jul. 26, 1811 Berks County Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Kilmer (Nikolaus Kulmer, with 2 dots over the u) was the son of Abraham Kilmer (Kullmer)(1717- 1756) and Anna Eva Laucks (1717-1772). He was of German descent but was born in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. He was a tailor by
2 CONC  trade when he left Philadelphia for Berks County, where he apparently did well for himself. Nicholas married Elizabeth Thiess (Tice) on December 13, 1763 in Berks County. He and Elizabeth went on to have many children, the third 
2 CONC eldest child and third son was Jonathan, my 4th Ggrandfather. Jonathan is buried at Tulpehocken Trinity UCC Cemetery, so I'm hoping that Nicholas is too. The children of Nicholas and Elizabeth were: David (1764-1843), Michael (176
2 CONC 7-1773),Jonathan (1769-1836) Eve, Barbara (who married Benjamen Lauer), Magdalena (who married Andrew Katterman), Elizabeth (who married Valentine Uhrich), Eve (who married Michael Uhrich), David and Nicholas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   Abraham Kilmer (1717 - 1756)
2 CONT   Anna Eva Laucks Kilmer
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Elizabeth Thiess Kilmer (1739 - 1831)*
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Updated from [http://trees.ancestry.com/tree/13443338/person/1959202597 Ancestry Genealogy] via son [http://www.geni.com/profile-34675814730 Jonathan Kilmer] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 15 
2 CONC 2015, 14:56:15 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Nicholas Kilmer (Nikolaus Kulmer, with 2 dots over the u) was the son of Abraham  Kilmer  (Kullmer)(1717- 1756) and Anna Eva Laucks (1717-1772). He was of German descent but was born in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. He was a tailor 
2 CONC by trade when he left Philadelphia for Berks County, where he apparently did well for himself.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Nicholas married Elizabeth Thiess (Tice) on December 13, 1763 in Berks County. He and Elizabeth went on to have many children, the third eldest child and third son was Jonathan, my 4th Ggrandfather. Jonathan is buried at Tulpehoc
2 CONC ken Trinity UCC Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Nicholas and Elizabeth were: David (1764-1843), Michael (1767-1773),Jonathan (1769-1836) Eve,  Barbara (who married Benjamen Lauer), Magdalena (who married Andrew Katterman), Elizabeth (who married Valentine Uhrich
2 CONC ), Eve (who married Michael Uhrich), David and Nicholas.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/65141476/nicholas-kilmer Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 16 2019, 
