1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Urbana Fanny Conrad Hammer BIRTH	8 Mar 1853 DEATH	9 Jun 1939 (aged 86) BURIAL	 Ruddle Presbyterian Church Cemetery Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA  MEMORIAL ID	106760197
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/106760197
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Taylor Hammer was united in marriage December 7, 1878 with Miss Fannie Conrad, the only daughter of Laban and Rachel Conrad.
2 CONT
2 CONT A few years later they begin housekeeping on a small farm with no improvements.
2 CONT
2 CONT To this union were born 7 children, 2 daughters and 5 sons. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They worked both early and late, practiced economy, were honest and upright in all things and prospered, as their pennies accumulated they did not forget that God was the giver of all things and they gave freely of what they posse
2 CONC ssed to the church, the poor and the heathen and beautified their home.
2 CONT
2 CONT This home was one in which the neighbor, the visitor, the beggar and the stranger were always welcome, none ever left their door hungry or unaided in time of need.
