1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/80512604/lester-charles-hammer
2 CONT
2 CONT Lester Charles Hammer was born at Ruddle, Pendleton County, W.Va., on 10 Jan 1899, a son of Isaac Hammer and wife Arbana (or Urbana) Frances Conrad Hammer. He died at age 56 on 27 March 1956 in the Kanawha Valley Hospital, Charles
2 CONC ton, W.Va., after a three-month illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a graduate of the Valparaiso University, Ind., and the University of Akron School of Law in Ohio. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Hammer moved to Raleigh County, W.Va., in 1952 and married Dr. Eva L. Teter who had a practice in Beaver, W.Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had worked as a job analyst with the Ohio State Employment Office. Mr. Hammer owned and operated the Moon Glo Motel in Beaver which was constructed in 1955.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was survived by his wife and two sisters, Mrs. Mollie Bowers and Mrs. Bessie Bowers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Lester Hammer Rites Thursday, Post-Herald, Beckley, W.Va., 28 March 1956, Page 8, and L.C. Hammer, 56, Dies in Hospital, The Charleston Gazette, Charleston, W.Va., 28 March 1956, Page 8; and (birthdate) West Virginia, Dea
2 CONC ths Index, 1853-1973, FHL Film Number 460375.
