2 CONT Shirley Marie Kiser 1918-1993 m John Patrick Scanlon
2 CONT
2 CONT Graveside Service For Shirley Kiser
2 CONT
2 CONT    Shirley Trumbo Kiser, 94, of the Pendleton Nursing Home in Franklin died Sunday at Rockingham Memorial Hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Mrs. Kiser was born June 7, 1890, in Brandywine, and was a daughter of the late Morgan Gilbert and Mary Catherine Byrd Trumbo.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Mrs. Kiser lived for 54 years at Greeley, Colo., prior to moving to the nursing home.
2 CONT
2 CONT    She was a member of the First Christian Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Her husband, Harry H. Kiser, died July 23, 1972.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Surviving are two daughters, Mrs. Chester (Mary Louise) Hiett of Great Cacapon and Mrs. J. Patrick (S. Marie) Scanlon of Winchester, Va.;  a son Raymond T. Kiser of Las Cruces, N.M.;  and four grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT    A graveside service was conducted 11 a.m. Tuesday at the Pine Hill Cemetery in Brandywine by the Rev. Maynard Baker.  Internment was by the Basagic Funeral Home.
