1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Aud graduated from Dunsmore Business College in Staunton, VA and moved south to his first job, as a bookkeeper, where he died of typhoid fever.  His body was later moved to Pine Hill Cemetery in Brandywine, WV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Letter from Aud to his mother posted 7 October 1902 from Welch, WV to Brandywine, WV.  He died 18 October 1902.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dear Mother
2 CONT      The doctor says I have typhoid fever at last and I am writing to you while laying in bed.  Don't be uneasy about me for I am going to the hospital and have a trained nurse and will get along just as well if at home.  I haven'
2 CONC t heard from any of you for about 2 weeks.  I don't know what is wrong.  Has Papa said anything to Carter about my trunk.  Tell Papa to tell Carter to push things a little far.  I will soon want my trunk. Hope Shirley is better.
2 CONT      With much love to all
2 CONT      I am your son Aud Don't be uneasy about me momma (words underlined)
