2 CONT Lon  D. Trumbo, Retired County Merchant, Dies
2 CONT
2 CONT Lon Dyer Trumbo, 85, of Brandywine, a former Pendleton County sheriff and prominent citizen, died Tuesday evening at Bridgewater, Va.  Mr. Trumbo operated a gereral store at Brandywine for many years until his retirement several y
2 CONC ears ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born at Sugar Grove November 29, 1882, a son of Morgan G. and Mary Catherine Byrd Trumbo.  He was married to Mary Jane Bowers who preceded him in death on December 22, 1957.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Trumbo is survived by a daughter, Mrs. R. H. (Dorothy) Boggs of Franklin;  two sisters Miss Cleda Trumbo of Brandywine, and Mrs. Harry (Shirley) Kiser of Greeley, Colorado;  a brother, Dr. G. C. Trumbo of Norfolk, Va.;  three 
2 CONC grandchildren and three great-grandchildren.  He was preceded in death by  daughter, a brother  and a sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT A funeral service will be conducted Friday morning at 11 o’clock at the Brandywine Christian Church by the Rev. J. E. Reynolds of Brandywine and the Rev. J. Wilson Rowe, of Franklin, and interment will in Pine Hill Cemetery at Bra
2 CONC ndywine.
