2 CONT Cleda Trumbo, Past Brandywine Postmaster, Dies
2 CONT
2 CONT Miss Cleda Trumbo. 95, of Brandywine, a former Brandywine postmaster, died Monday in Pendleton Nursing Home in Franklin where she had resided for the past two years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Miss Trumbo served as postmaster of Brandywine Post Office from 1942 to 1959 and she was county supervisor of Women’s WPA Program in Pendleton County in the 1930s.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a charter member of the Pendleton Order of Eastern Star and a member of the Brandywine Christian Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born at Brandywine February 14, 1888, and was a daughter of the late Morgan G. and Mary Catherine Byrd Trumbo.  She was never married.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by a sister, Mrs. Harry (Shirley) Kiser, a resident of Pendleton Nursing Home, six nieces and two nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT A funeral service will be held this morning at 11 o’clock at the Brandywine Christian Church by the Rev. Russell Jarvis, and interment will be in Pine Hill Cemetery in Brandywine by Basagic Funeral Home.
2 CONT
2 CONT In lieu of flowers, the family has requested that memorials be made to Pendleton Nursing Home.
