1 NAME Edward Pugh /Chenoweth/
2 GIVN Edward Pugh
2 SURN Chenoweth
2 _MARNM Chenoweth
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1823
2 ADDR
3 CITY Chenoweth Creek, Beverly
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 5 JUL 1863
2 PLAC location of death unknown
2 ADDR
1 OCCU farmer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Additional Curator's Notes:===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Regarding the death of Edward Pugh Chenoweth at Fort Delaware --''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chenoweth Family Association believes that Pugh Chenoweth was picked up by the Union Army in Randolph County, Virginia (later West Virginia) and taken as a civilian hostage, then was transported to Fort Delaware, where he died
2 CONC . This is partly based on the book ''A history of Randolph County, West Virginia, from its earliest exploration and settlement to the present time,'' by Dr. A. S. Bosworth, and published 1916 in Elkins, West Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have been corresponding with one of the board members for the Fort Delaware Society regarding this matter. They have no record of Pugh being held prisoner at Fort Delaware. Of the party of men described in Dr. Bosworth's book, [
2 CONC Lenox Camden, William Salisbury, and his son --- Salisbury, Pugh Chenoweth, Levi Ward, Allen Isner, Philip Isner, William Clemm, Smith Crouch, Thomas Crouch, John Caplinger, John Leary and Charles Russell], only five were actually
2 CONC  at Fort Delaware - William Salisbury, Smith Crouch, Levi Ward, Allen Isner and Phillip Isner. Dr. Bosworth claimed they all died in prison except for last four. Of this group of men from Randolph County, only Allen Isner and Smit
2 CONC h Crouch died at the prison.
2 CONT
2 CONT So what happened to Pugh Chenoweth? We do know that he was arrested by Union soldiers on July 5, 1863 for "disloyalty." We have a document proving the arrest. After that, there are no records for Pugh.  Here are my theories
2 CONT *He was headed for Fort Delaware with his friends and died along the way. These Southern sympathizers were sometimes placed in chain gangs and forced to do hard labor before their transfer to prisoner of war camps and prisons.
2 CONT *His friend Levi Dyer Ward was sent first to Atheneum Prison in Charleston, and from there, sent to Camp Chase, near Columbus, Ohio, before being transferred to Fort Delaware. Pugh may have been sent to Atheneum with Levi and died
2 CONC  along the way.
2 CONT *Camp Chase has excellent records, and their own Confederate cemetery.  I can't find a Pugh Chenoweth there. Atheneum, on the other hand, was a converted warehouse and theatre. I have not been able to find a list of prisoners held
2 CONC  there or where any dead prisoners would have been buried.  Pugh could have been sent there and died in Charleston.
2 CONT
2 CONT All we really know about the death of Edward Pugh Chenoweth is that he was picked up in Randolph County by Union forces on July 5, 1863 and never heard from again.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Edmonds-Zediker, Volunteer Curator, February 12, 2014.
2 CONT
2 CONT  ************************************************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT '''EDWARD PUGH CHENOWETH  1824-1863'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Edward Pugh Chenoweth''' was born in Randolph Co., Virginia.  He was the third son and fourth child of Jehu and Eleanor 'Nelley' Skidmore Chenoweth. He married, at the age of 25, Martha Jane Salisbury, the daughter of William S
2 CONC alisbury and Lidia Crouch ( a few sites give her name as "Lizie"). He was generally known by his middle name, Pugh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pugh grew up to be one of the leading citizens of Beverly. According to family lore, during the Civil War, Pugh, with his father-in-law William Salisbury, William's brother-in-law Smith Crouch and ten other citizens of the county,
2 CONC  were taken as a civilian hostages by Union forces and sent to Fort Delaware Prison, Pea Patch Island, Delaware. Family lore also has it that Pugh, William Salisbury and Smith Crouch all died there during their internment. Martha 
2 CONC was left to raise the family of five children.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1870s, the children relocated to Preston Co., WV. They then went to Garrett Co., MD before returning to Randolph Co., WV before 1900. Martha is buried in the IOOF, Midland cemetery, south of Elkins, Randolph Co., WV.
2 CONT
2 CONT *CENSUS: 1850 VA: Randolph Co: 52nd district: page 71, 1860 VA: Randolph Co, Beverly PO: page 5, (widow, Martha) 1870 WV: Preston Co: Lyon twp: page 122, 1880 MD: Garrett Co: Bloomington: page 318D, 1900 WV: Randolph Co: Leadsvill
2 CONC e: page 101, 1910 WV: Randolph Co: Leadville district, Elkins City: page 20 
2 CONT *LOCATIONS: Randolph Co., VA (now WV) 
2 CONT *BOOKS: Harris pages 69-70, Hiatt page 50, Katherine Frame: Harts of Randolph 
2 CONT *OTHER SOURCES: Family of Edward Pugh research of David W. Biser, Phares File: Richard Phares, Phyllis, wife of Robert Chenoweth, Debbie Chenoweth Koza, Debbie Jones, Kathy L. Russell Brown, Betty Ridenour Minnear, Linda Harper Jo
2 CONC nes, research of Phyllis Daniels and Okey Lee McQuain, Census Work 1880-1910, WFT Vol 4 # 3273 
2 CONT *OTHER COUSIN CONTACTS: Betty Minnear Childers, Ronald L Robe, Val Sawhill
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of EDWARD PUGH CHENOWETH and MARTHA SALISBURY are:
2 CONT * Christopher Columbus b. May 29, 1851, Randolph Co., VA (now WV); d. March 27, 1927, Morgantown, Monongalia Co., WV; m. LURAINE 'LULU' SHUTTLESWORTH, May 15, 1876, Preston Co., WV; b. November 1853, Preston Co., VA (now WV); d. A
2 CONC ugust 01, 1911, Bayard, Grant Co., WV.
2 CONT * William Mandeville b. July 27, 1853, Beverly, Randolph Co., VA (now WV); d. December 30, 1930, Homestead, Allegheny Co., PA; m. AMANDA WINDLE, August 14, 1883; b. February 24, 1857, Pennsylvania; d. September 04, 1956, Morgantow
2 CONC n, Monongalia Co., WV.
2 CONT * Rachel Ellen b. October 22, 1855, Randolph Co., VA (now WV); d. Aft. 1927; m. ZACHARIAH THOMAS MINNEAR, October 05, 1872, Austin, Preston Co., WV; b. March 09, 1849, Fairmont, Marion Co., WV; d. July 31, 1923, Akron, Summit Co.,
2 CONC  OH.
2 CONT * Mary 'Mollie' b. November 15, 1857, Randolph Co., WV; d. Unknown; m. THOMAS J. BELL, May 15, 1878, Garrett Co., MD; b. July 1854, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT * Eli Pugh b. September 29, 1861, Randolph Co., WV; d. Unknown; m. AGNES B. ?, Abt. 1894; b. August 1860, Virginia
2 CONT
