1 NOTE {geni:about_me} George H. Owens, 83 (1860-1944), poet laureate of Henry County and for fifty years cashier of the Citizens Bank of Port Royal, died at his home in Port Royal at 6 p.m., Tuesday, following an illness of several year
2 CONC s.  He resigned as cashier of the bank in 1937 and retired.
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased was called on many times during his active life to write poetry for various occasions.  His best poems; however, were of a personal nature such as the one published in the Local in November, 1937, about the time he de
2 CONC cided to retire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were conducted at the residence at 2 p.m., Thursday, with Rev. J. W. Parrish officiating.  Burial was in the Port Royal Cemetery.  He was a member of the Christian Church and the Masonic Lodge.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife: Mrs. Mae Sadifer Owens; two daughters: Mrs. J. M. Schultz, Wauchula, FL and Mrs. A. M. Honaker, Port Royal; one son: Cpl. Robert S. Owens, stationed in the Aleutian Islands.  Six grandchildren also surv
2 CONC ive.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry County Local  September 8, 1944
