1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Evidence needed to support as daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Jagely-Jacob-B%C3%A4r/6000000000933343922?through=6000000001896007055
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Maria Eva Bear 
2 CONT * BIRTH	1709 Telford, Montgomery County, Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT *  DEATH	1771 (aged 61–62) Forestville, Shenandoah County, Virginia, USA 
2 CONT * BURIAL	 Zirkle Cemetery New Market, Shenandoah County, Virginia,
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed origins 
2 CONT < [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bär-198 Wikitree] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT >There is no documented proof that Jagley Bär married Mary Wilson nor had a daughter named Maria Eva Bear Zirkle. Findagrave.com is a great resource, however, it does not required documented proof. I checked Jane Evans Best's Bear
2 CONC  Saga Update: Part Two. It did not list a wife for Jagley Bär nor a daughter for him. It was published by Pennsylvania Mennonite Heritage, Oct., 1998. I, also, checked The California Bare, Bear, Bar Family Tree:Index of Individual
2 CONC s by Jonathan Bare. Again no Mary Wilson nor Maria Eva Bear Zirkle.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/50531349/maria-eva-zirkle
2 CONT
2 CONT death place could have been Shenandoah Co. VA need to look for sure
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Eva BEAR1 was born about 1709 in Europe, came to Amer. in 1725. She died in 1771 in Forestville, New Market, VA 1776?. She was buried in Forestville Cemetery, Shenandoah Co., VA. Children's last names Zerckel, Zirckel, and Z
2 CONC irckle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Zirkel m.c. 1748 to a Chriss Ottinger in Montgomery Co., PA. By 1750 he was deceased and by 1755 Maria was in Rockingham Co., VA with some of her children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Lodowich (Ludwig) Zirkle and Maria Eva BEAR had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * +15 i. Catherine ZIRCKLE. 
2 CONT * 16 ii. Michael Zerkel or ZIRKLE1 was born on 29 Jan 1735 in Telford, Franconia Twp, PA. He was baptized in 1755. He died on 2 Oct 1811 in Forestville, Shenandoah Co., VA. He was buried in Nease/Zirkle graveyard, Forestville, Va.
2 CONC  May have lived in the Forestville, Holman Creek, VA area. One source says he is possibly buried in Rockingham Co., VA.
2 CONT *  17 iii. Margaret ZIRCKLE5,1 was born on 6 Mar 1736 in Pennsylvania. She was baptized in 1755. She died in 1796 in New Market, Shenandoah Co., VA. According to the register of Indianfield Lutheran Church in Franconia Twp., Montg
2 CONC omery Co., PA, Michael and Margaret were married March 6, 1753. They were the parents of 9 children. Don Ottinger lists her name as Virginia Margareta Zerkelsen (Zirkle).
2 CONT *  18 iv. Andrew Zirckel or ZIRCKLE1 was born in 1737 in Telford, Montgomery Co., PA. He died in 1816 in Forestville, Shenandoah Co., VA. He was buried in Forestville, Shenandoah Co., VA. He was baptized in Forestville, Shenandoah
2 CONC  Co., VA. Betty Zirkle says birth date is 1727. 
2 CONT * +19 v. George Adam Zirckel or ZIRCKLE. 
2 CONT * 20 vi. Lewis (Ludwig) ZIRKLE1 was born in 1740 in Telford, Montgomery Co., PA. He was baptized in 1755 in New Market, Shenandoah Co., VA. He died on 22 Jan 1815 in New Market, Shenandoah Co., VA. Born 1736-1740. Married 1764 - 1
2 CONC 768. Born in Pennsylvania?
2 CONT *  +21 vii. Peter Circle ZIRCKLE. 
2 CONT *.22 viii. William ZIRKLE1 was born about 1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT She was buried in Zirkle Cemetery, near Forestville, Shenandoah County, Virginia. She, two daughters, and five sons moved to near 'the Forest,' now known as Forestville, in what then was Augusta County, Virginia (and now is Shenan
2 CONC doah County), probably in August 1753. In 1755 she obtained a grant or patent for seventy-five acres on a branch of the Shenandoah River; the warrant for the survey, which was made in late 1754, said that this land adjoined other 
2 CONC land she owned. They may have lived around Culpeper, in East Virginia, for a year or so before settling in the Shenandoah Valley. She had no children by her marriage to Christopher Ottinger. She probably was buried in the Zirkle g
2 CONC raveyard on the east bank of Holman's Creek, which now is a pasture without grave markers, about one mile northeast of Forestville.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	1709 Telford Montgomery County Pennsylvania, USA Death: 	1771 Forestville Shenandoah County Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Eva Bear was the daughter of Jack Baer and Mary Wilson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Some folks say that Maria Eva Bear was born in Germany and then immigrated to America in 1725.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria, a Lutheran, married Johann Ludwig Zirkle during 1725 in Telford, Franconia Twp., Montgomery Co., PA. They had 8 children they named George Henry, Catherine, Michael, Maria Margareta, Andrew, George Adam, Ludwig Lewis and Pe
2 CONC ter Circle Zirkle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria was married a second time after Ludwig's death. She married Christopher Ottinger in 1748. Since there are no markers in the cemetery, we have no way of knowing whether she would have been buried as a Zirkle or an Ottinger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
