2 CONT Johann a farmer was the son of Heinrich Zirkle and Eva Euphrosina Rezin of Germany. Like his parents and wife he was a Lutheran. He immigrated to America at the age of 19 during the year 1725. "Families of Gallia County" Ludwig wa
2 CONC s a saddler who came to PA in 1725 from Ittlingen, near Heidelberg, Germany. Bought land in 1735 on the NE branch of Perkiomen Creek in Montgomery Co, PA near today's Norristown. His widow and their 5 sons went to the Shenandoah V
2 CONC alley where they all bought property near today's Harrisonburg and New Market, VA. George Adam's property was closer to Timberville. some descendats still own the Luray Caverns.
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Early Gallia County Records' 1734 Philadelphia Co Taxables Ludwig Zerke
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Lodowich (Ludwig) Zirkle1 was born on 9 Oct 1705 in Ittlingen, Baden, Germany. He died about Jan 1747 in Telford, Pennsylvania. He was buried in Indian Fields Lutheran Churchyard, Philadelphia, PA. Twin of Anne Mary. To Ame
2 CONC rican 1725 on Brittannia and located in PA. Some information confirmed 10/23/94 by Ron Cline who looked it up in ZIRKLE FAMILY HISTORY by J. William Harpine 1963. Book as Lodowick's last will and testament, etc. Lived for many yea
2 CONC rs in Forestville, Shenandoah County, Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Maria Eva BEAR about 1732 in Telford, PA.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~kycarter/charts/circle_zurckel.pdf
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT His first name may have been Johann. He probably had a son, George Henry Zirkle, by an earlier marriage in Germany. He came to America in 1725 with his father and twin sister. He owned some land in Pennsylvania, and they farmed ne
2 CONC ar Telford, in the Philadelphia area. The Rising Sun Inn, built in 1739, a short distance from Little Zion Church in Telford, stands on his land. They were Lutherans, and he gave one acre of land to be used for a Lutheran church '
2 CONC so long as soon a moon a shining' (so long as the sun and moon shine). He was a farmer and saddler.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=angiesmith&id=I1809
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I1809 Name: Johann Ludwig Zirkle 1 Sex: M Birth: 9 OCT 1705 in Ittlingen, Baden, Germany 1 Death: 10 MAR 1747 in Franconia, Montgomery, Pennsylvania 2 Death: 1747 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA 1 Burial: 1747 Little Zion L
2 CONC utheran Church Cemetery, Earlington, Montgomery, Pennsylvania 2 Census: Parents: Heinrich Zirkle 2 Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Johann a farmer was the son of Heinrich Zirkle and Eva Euphrosina Rezin of Germany. Like his parents and wife he was a Lutheran. He immgrated to America at the age of 19 during the year 1725.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Johann Ludwig Zirkle married Maria Eva Bear during 1725 in Telford, Franconia Twp., Montgomery Co., PA. They had 8 children they named George Henry, Catherine, Michael, Maria Margareta, Andrew, George Adam, Ludwig Lewis and Pe
2 CONC ter Circle Zirkle.
2 CONT
2 CONT     http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=50532716
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth: 	Oct. 9, 1705 Baden-Baden, Germany Death: 	Mar. 10, 1747 Franconia Montgomery County Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann or John a farmer was the son of Heinrich Zirkle and Eva Euphrosina Rezin of Germany. Like his parents and wife he was a Lutheran. He immgrated to America at the age of 19 during the year 1725.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a brother also named Johann who likely went by the name John in America. It is believed that our/this Johann actually went by the nick name of "Lewis".
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Ludwig Zirkle, "Lewis", married Maria Eva Bear during 1725 in Telford, Franconia Twp., Montgomery Co., PA. They had 8 children they named George Henry, Catherine, Michael, Maria Margareta, Andrew, George Adam, Ludwig Lewis 
2 CONC and Peter Circle Zirkle.
2 CONT
2 CONT April 2013 Burial Comments - Betsy Snook from the Little Zion Lutheran Church
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Ludwig Zirkle donated the land for the church and cemetery called the "Little Zion Lutheran Church Cemetery" (Indianfield Graveyard) in Montgomery Co., PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT However; upon his death he was buried in the Fuhrman Cemetery which was located at GPS 40 19 19.69 N 75 20 49.36W - Very near the Little Zion Lutheran Church Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fuhrman Cemetery is no longer in existence. It seems that the cemetery was eventually plowed into farmland and there is now a housing development located on the site.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of the markers from the old Fuhrman cemetery have shown up for sale. The Little Zion Church has acquired some of these markers and have put them together in the Zion Lutheran Church Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Ludwig Zirkle & Maria Eva Bear Husband: Johann Ludwig Zirkle Bapt.: 09 Oct 1705 in Ittlingen, , Baden-Württemberg, Germany (1 2) Married:
2 CONT  in , , PA, USA Died: before 17 Jan 1746/47 in Franconia, Mongomery, PA, USA (3) Father: Johann Heinrich Zirkle Mother: Eva Euphrosina Resin Wife: Maria Eva Bear Born: about 1715 Died: before 1776 in Forestville, Shenandoah, VA, U
2 CONC SA (4) Children: 01  (M): George Henry Zirkle Born: about 1731 Died: Unknown 02  (F): Catherine Zirkle Born: 06 Apr 1733 Died: 04 Jan 1817 03  (M): Michael Zirkle Born: 29 Jan 1734/35 Died: 02 Oct 1811 04  (F): Margaret Zirkle Bor
2 CONC n: 06 Mar 1735/36 Died: 1796 05  (M): Andrew Zirkle Born: about 1737 Died: before 10 Jun 1816 in Forestville, Shenandoah, VA, USA Spouse: Mary Catherine 06  (M): George Adam Zirkle Born: about 1738 Died: before 08 Sep 1800 07  (M)
2 CONC : Lewis Zirkle Born: about 1740 Died: 22 Jan 1815 08  (M): Peter Zirkle Born: about 1741 Died: about Sep 1818 More Info: Johann Ludwig Zirkle:
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: In the name of God. Amen. The Twenty Eight day of 8 bris 1746. I being sick and weak in body, but of perfect mind and memory Thanks be given unto God, therefore calling to mind the mortality of my Body and knowing that it is
2 CONC  appointed for all men once to die do make and ordain this my last Will and Testament That is to say - principally and first of all I give and recommend my Soul into the Hands of God who gave it and for my Body I recommend it to t
2 CONC he Earth to be buried in a Christian like and decent manner at the discretion of my Executor nothing doubting that at the General Ressurrection I shall receive the same again by the mighty power of God and as touching such worldly
2 CONC  Estate wherewith it hath pleased God to bless me in this life, I give devise and dispose of the same in the following manner and form Imprimis it is my Will and I do order that in the first place my Wife Maria Eva is to have all 
2 CONC my Estate both Real and Personalities till my youngest child are twelve years old. Item after my decease my Loving Executors hereafter named is to have full power to Sell all my Real and Personalities if they find it necessary as 
2 CONC if I was present to pay all my just debts and funeral charges be paid and satisfied and the remaining part of money is to be put one Interest by my Executors Item Maria Eva my Loving Wife is to have the Furth of all, the two Furth
2 CONC s amongst my children in Equal share, Except my Eldest Son George Henry is to have for his portion Twenty Five Pounds weil hewend four years before his Each to learn a Treath to be paid when he have set up for himself. Item if my 
2 CONC Wife shall marry, then all my Estate is to be sold by my Executors afternamed. Item I give to my Trusty Friend Peter Snider and my well beloved Wife Maria Eva whom I likewise Constitute make and ordain my sole Executors of this my
2 CONC  Last Will and Testament all and singular in presents In Witness whereof I have hereunto Set my Hand and Seal on the day and year above written. Lodowick Zirkle (L.S.) Signed Sealed Published Pronounced and declared by the said Lo
2 CONC dowick Zirkle as his Last Will and Testament in the presence of us. Henry (his O mark) Seible Andrew Bernhart
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: I being sick and weak in body bit of perfect mind and memor y thanks being to God. Wife, Maria Eva to have all of my es tatee, both real and personalties till my youngest child 1 2 years old.After my decease my loving execut
2 CONC ors after name d is to have full power to sell all of my real estate and p ersonalties if he finds necessary. Maria Evamy loving wif e is to have the furth of all, the two furths among my chil drenin equal shares except my oldest 
2 CONC son George Henry is t o have his for his portion 25 pounds. Weil hewend 4 years b efore his each to learn a Treath to be paid when he hath se t up for himself. If my wife marries then all of my estat e to be sold by my executors, 
2 CONC or trusty friend Peter Snide r and well belovedwife Maria Eva, executors. Lodowick Zirkle Wintess: Henry Seible - Andrew Barnhardt __ [Francony township] Be it know that I, Lodowick Zirckle , in Franconia Township that long time a
2 CONC goe have given an d bequeathed one acre of landfor the use of the prober Luth eran Church where the congreation have build upon one churc h. She is to have and to hold said decsribed so long as soo n a moon a shining, for no tothe
2 CONC r use then for the said pro ber Evangilly LutheranChurch and have a Deed, being in Fran conia township the 28th day 8bris, 1746. At probate Salford Jan. 17, 1746. Peter Shneider Andrew Bar nhardt HenrySeible Philadelphia Co., Deed
2 CONC s, PA (From origin al record)
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ludwig was listed as a tanner by trade and a Lutheran. He and Eva lived in Franconia Twp., near Philadelphia, PA, on more than 200 acres which bordered Branch Creek.  In his will, Ludwig mentions the Indianfield (Little Zion) Luth
2 CONC eran Church: "Be it known that I, Lodowick Zirkle in Frankonia Township, now in my sickness, being in remembrance that I, a long time ago, bequeathed one acre of my land for the use of the Lutheran Church, to have and to hold the 
2 CONC said described so long as the Sun and Moon are Shining. (Philadelphia Will Book H, p.209) After Ludwig's death, Eve married Christopher Hottinger, and he died within a couple of years. Maria and her children moved to near 'the For
2 CONC est,' now known as Forestville, in what then was Augusta County, Virginia (and now is Shenandoah County), probably in August 1753. In 1755 she obtained a grant or patent for seventy-five acres on a branch of the Shenandoah River; 
2 CONC the warrant for the survey, which was made in late 1754, said that this land adjoined other land she owned. Ludwig mentions eldest son George Henry in his will, probably from an earlier marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ref: Little Zion Lutheran Church, 1730-1970
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Johann or John a farmer was the son of Heinrich Zirkle and Eva Euphrosina Rezin of Germany. Like his parents and wife he was a Lutheran. He immgrated to America at the age of 19 during the year 1725.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a brother also named Johann who likely went by the name John in America. It is believed that our/this Johann actually went by the nick name of "Lewis".
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Ludwig Zirkle, "Lewis", married Maria Eva Bear during 1725 in Telford, Franconia Twp., Montgomery Co., PA. They had 8 children they named George Henry, Catherine, Michael, Maria Margareta, Andrew, George Adam, Ludwig Lewis 
2 CONC and Peter Circle Zirkle.
2 CONT
2 CONT April 2013 Burial Comments - Betsy Snook from the Little Zion Lutheran Church
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Ludwig Zirkle donated the land for the church and cemetery called the "Little Zion Lutheran Church Cemetery" (Indianfield Graveyard) in Montgomery Co., PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT However; upon his death he was buried in the Fuhrman Cemetery which was located at GPS 40 19 19.69 N 75 20 49.36W - Very near the Little Zion Lutheran Church Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fuhrman Cemetery is no longer in existence. It seems that the cemetery was eventually plowed into farmland and there is now a housing development located on the site.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of the markers from the old Fuhrman cemetery have shown up for sale. The Little Zion Church has acquired some of these markers and have put them together in the Zion Lutheran Church Cemetery.
2 CONT
