2 CONT <p>Home in 1850</p><p>(City,County,State):    District 38, Mason, Virginia </p><p>Name:    Daniel Roush </p><p>Age:    62 </p><p>Estimated birth year:    abt 1788 </p><p>Birth place:    Virginia </p><p>Gender:    Male </p><p>Page:
2 CONC     406 </p><p>Roll:    M432_959 </p><p>---------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>&nbsp</p><p>Nancy Clay lpclay@cwv.net found 9-18-2002</p><p>&nbsp</p><p>&nbsp</p><p> Daniel was born Decembe
2 CONC r 01, 1787 in Shenandoah Co., VA. He was the fourth son of George and Catherine (Zerkle) Roush.Daniel married Catherine Yeager, January 02, 1810 in Mason co., W(VA) in a place called Pleasant Flats. Daniel's children are George Jr
2 CONC ., born 1810, Mary A. born 1812, Peter born 1814, Sarah, Samuel born 1818, Daniel born December 27, 1821, Joseph Albert born 1827, and I don't see any more at the moment. He had a lot of children like his father. George and Cather
2 CONC ine Zerkle Roush are my ggg grandparents.</p><p>-------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>FROM "THE ROUSH FAMILY IN AMERICA" VOLUME I, PAGE 476, 477</p><p>He was a lad of only eleven years of 
2 CONC age when, in 1798, he came with his parents to Mason County (now WV), settling in the Ohio Valley near the present site of Graham Station. He spent his younger days with his father on the Roush estate in Mason County. In the Mason
2 CONC  County records for October, 1805, Daniel Roush is credited with payment of bounty for the scalp of one grown wolf. On January 2, 1810, he was united in marriage to Catharine Yeager of the same county, the ceremony occurring at wh
2 CONC at was then known as Pleasant Flats. Catharine Yeager was born October 4, 1790.</p><p>Daniel Roush enlisted at Point Pleasant, Virginia, September 28, 1812, and served as private in Captain A. Van Sickle's Company of Colonel Dudle
2 CONC y Evans' Second Regiment in the First Brigade of Virginia Militia. This company saw a great deal of active service on and about Lake Erie. He was discharged March 27, 1813. (See Lewis Roush of this chapter).</p><p>Farming was his 
2 CONC vocation and this occupation he followed all his life.</p><p>Daniel Roush was one of the founders of the White Church (Lutheran), the first church in Graham District, established in the year 1820 by the Rev. Gideon Henkel, who was
2 CONC  its first pastor. This building, a few miles back of New Haven, was erected of hewed logs and its dimensions were 20 by 24 feet, the extent of the structure was sufficient to provide a seating capacity for about fifty people. Oth
2 CONC er members of the Roush family aiding in the founding of this church were Anthony Roush, son of Henry; Catharine, daughter of George; Abraham, son of Jonas and Elizabeth Roush. The body of Daniel Roush was interred in the churchya
2 CONC rd burial plot adjacent to the church, at the time of his death.</p>At the time of his death, which occurred in Mason County, WV, September 2, 1866, at which time he was aged 79 years, he is said to have owned 400 acres of land. T
2 CONC he widow of Daniel Roush died July 28, 1886, at the advanced age of 96 years.
2 CONT
