2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT !From Roush bk, Vol I: "Lewis Roush was one of the Mason County soldiers of the War of 1812."  He became part of the group known as "Mason County Riflemen."  "This company was assigned to the 2nd Virginia Regiment, commanded by Co
2 CONC lonel Dudley Evans, and was sent to the Maume Rapids, where it formed a junction of the army under the command of Wm. Henry Harrison.  They erected Fort Meigs at which place they were mustered out of service in 1813."
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT <p>Veteran War of 1812</p> <p>&amp;nbsp</p> <p>1870 Mason County Census also lists in household, his daughter Mary and two of her children, George &amp; Charles E. Nease (Spelled Niece) age 10 &amp; 4.</p>
