1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=10317141-4-14617&action=showRecord MyHeritage Family Trees] via brother [http://www.geni.com/profile-34671170700 Giles 
2 CONC Elijah Gordin] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 14 2015, 7:10:11 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine (Gordon) Leffel was born on May 15, 1817, in Bethel Township, Clark County, Ohio. She married Samuel Leffel on November 2, 1837, in Clark County, Ohio. Catherine passed away on November 29, 1906, in Wabash County, Indian
2 CONC a, at the age of 88. She was the mother of twelve children, including Jacob B. LEFFEL; Lucinda LEFFEL; Annie LEFFEL; David LEFFEL; John Sheran LEFFEL; Joshua LEFFEL; William Benton LEFFEL; Josiah LEFFEL; Andrew Gordon LEFFEL; Sara
2 CONC  Jane LEFFEL; Lydia Belle LEFFEL and Lida Eliza LEFFEL.
2 CONT
2 CONT ——-
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Gordon & Anna Garst had seventeen children, and raised all but one to maturity. Pages 124-147 of Our Garst Family in America cover some of their descendants. I am only entering enough to show their descendent who married i
2 CONC nto our other lines.
2 CONT
2 CONT Early Clark County  Families, Vol. V, p. 3, entry submitted by Betty E. Hendrickson, 3462 Moraga Blvd., Lafayette, CA 94549 1850 census of Clark
2 CONT County, Bethel twp, page 120, enumerated Aug 22, lists this  family as #970:
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Gordon, 75; Anna, 65. Both born in Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the state of Washington there is a town named Gorst, and in that town there are people named Gharst, and also people named Garst. A professor of the University in Holland told Rev. John Newton Garst that the name meant “Grain D
2 CONC ealer,” and that our ancestors many years ago were evidently importers and exporters of grain, such as wheat, barley, and rye.
