1 NOTE {geni:about_me} per The Northville Record, 2 Nov 1923:
2 CONT "Mrs. E. K. Simonds, one of Northville's oldest residents, passed away, in Plymouth . . . last Thursday, aged 85 years.
2 CONT Adaline Ovenshire was born on a farm in the township of Novi, Oakland county, November 7th, 1838. When a young girl she moved to Northville, and resided there until her marriage to George B. Morse, December 15th, 1858. They moved 
2 CONC to Holly, where Mr. Morse's death occurred March 5th, 1863, when Mrs. Morse returned to Northville, and resided with her parents, Mr. and Mrs. John Ovenshire, until her marriage to Capt. E. K. Simonds, which took place October 13t
2 CONC h, 1880."
2 CONT Contributor: Susan (50061687)
