2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 20 OCT 1819
2 PLAC Chester County, South Carolina, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 JUL 1867
2 PLAC Franklin County, Alabama, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Silas was the youngest son of fourteen children born to Martin Kee and Eleanor Daniel.  He had three sisters younger than himself.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Plaiscetta Adeline Culp, the daughter of Johan/John Culp and Sarah Jordan, about 1840 in Chester Co., South Carolina.  John Silas and Plaiscetta had nine children, five girls and four boys.
2 CONT
2 CONT After John Silas' death, probably about 1875, Plaiscetta moved to Texas with five of her nine children.  The two oldest girls married Underwoods and remained in Alabama.  Joseph died unknown date and is also buried in Abston Cemet
2 CONC ery.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Plaiscetta's oldest son, Richard Brannon Kee, had already moved to Texas some time after 1872, when his daughter, Mary Plaiscetta was born.  His next child, Harvey Gilmore, was born 1875 in Texas.* Reference: [https://www
2 CONC .findagrave.com/memorial/30317993/john-silas-kee Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 16 2020, 17:05:42 UTC''
2 CONT
