1 NAME Mary “Polly” Rose /Auvenshine/
2 GIVN Mary “Polly” Rose
2 SURN Auvenshine
2 _MARNM Boyles
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Rhome
3 STAE TX
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1 JAN 1860
2 ADDR
3 STAE Tennessee
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 3 APR 1879
2 ADDR
3 CITY Aurora
3 STAE Texas
3 POST 76078
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daughter of William Elias Auvenshire b. 15 Jun 1827 in Warren Co., TN, and Gatsey Stoker.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary "Polly" married on 5 Jul 1877 in Jonesboro, TX, Joseph McKee Boyles b. 6 Dec 1852 in Sherman, Grayson Co., TX; they had one daughter: Elizabeth Gatsey Boyles b. 13 Jun 1878 in Jonesboro, TX, who married Franklin Preston Donat
2 CONC han b. 13 Jan 1867 in Revilee, Logan Co., AR.
2 CONT
2 CONT A letter written at the time of her death from her husband to his mother. Parts of the letter are missing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aurora, Wise Co. Tex.
2 CONT Apr. 4, 1879
2 CONT Dear & Affectionate Mother
2 CONT
2 CONT Your very welcome
2 CONT and interesting letter came to hand ********************** date which I am sad to s********************************** Rosie very ill she w************************************** hard chill on Saturday ******************************
2 CONC ***** followed which resulted in *******************************
2 CONT on Thursday following we have **************************** returned from the graveyard. She died as easy & quiet as if she was going to sleep. Mother you can have some idea what my feelings are to have my darling companion torn aw
2 CONC ay from me so very suddenly but Mother we all have to die sooner or later. I think Rosie was prepared ************** so my great loss was her great gain. Lizzie and myself are well hope you all are the same.
2 CONT
2 CONT Well Mother, I will let Mrs Auvenshine take Lizzie and keep her as for myself, I haven't decided what I will do I am to move our things to Mr Auvenshine's and as for your ******** I think probably John Thomas will take them if he 
2 CONC will I ******************************* take them down after while ************************************** him and let me know ******************************* was very glad to hear from ***********************************s him short
2 CONC ly. ********************************* I will close and await a ************** reply after which I will write again and do better.
2 CONT
2 CONT Write soon your affectionate son,
2 CONT yours with much love to all.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joe Boil
