1 NOTE {geni:about_me} excerpt from Loami Township in the Late 1800’s
2 CONT
2 CONT By Henry Clay Jones, As told to Lucy Miller Dodd
2 CONT
2 CONT http://sangamon.ilgenweb.net/twp-loahis2.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Polly Jones Dodd was from Tennessee - the only daughter of Joshua B. Jones of Tennessee. Uncle Charlie and Aunt Polly together with his brothers and families had moved to Illinois in 1852 and settled (some say 1851) south of Loami
2 CONC . My father, mother, Delila Edna, William, Jay and I think Mary Belle was a baby in my mothers arms, not sure, and myself. Together with an uncle Isaac M. Jones, wife and all of his family that was born then. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles and Mary Templeton Jones Dodd’s move to Illinois
2 CONT
2 CONT By Lucy Miller Dodd
2 CONT
2 CONT http://sangamon.ilgenweb.net/twp-loahis1.htm
