1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Individual Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Lucy Dodd Miller's notes: "Once when Uncle Josh lived east of South Fork School, where his children went, he got ready to go for them on horseback. It was pouring rain so he took the oil cloth off the dining table, cu
2 CONC t a hole in the middle and, putting it over his
2 CONT
2 CONT head, went forth. He got one child in front of him, the others behind, all under the oil cloth. Back home, the oil cloth finally spread over the table, he said, 'It's not much worse for the wear and tear.'
2 CONT
2 CONT Aunt Nancy went to Mo. to visit her people; when she came back, Uncle Josh had shaved clean. She told it and added, 'I was only gone 2 weeks and Joshua had shaved. Set out again '"
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hallgenealogy.com/ghtout/np36.htm#iin1279
