1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James Melvin Obenchain was born March 9, 1857 in Whitley Co., Indiana and died September 17, 1931 in Conway Springs, Kansas.
2 CONT The 1870 census shows James living with his parents at age 13 in Lawrenceville, Illinois. In 1881, a newspaper report states that he is sick with typhoid fever, but is slowly recovering. James was still a resident of Illinois at t
2 CONC his time.
2 CONT
2 CONT He marries Lydia Skiles December 9, 1883 in Piatt, Illinois. Some time before 1892, they move their family to the Conway Springs, Kansas area. A local newspaper article reports his troubles with asthma.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1900 census shows the couple living in Conway Springs on Monet Street, an that James is a salesman of dry goods and groceries. He owns his own home, free and clear.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1901, James puts up his home in Conway Springs for sale. The house has three acres, six rooms, a pump in the kitchen and a root cellar.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1903, James opens a business with George Mead, Obenchain and Mead, seller of dry goods and groceries in Conway Springs.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Conway Springs Star, August 28, 1903
2 CONT
2 CONT James Obenchain and George Mead will open a grocery store in the room on the corner east of Hubbard's store next week. The building is being thoroughly repaired for them and we believe they will do a nice business there. The firm 
2 CONC will be known as Obenchain & Mead.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1907, James and family sell their home and household items to move to Rocky Ford, Colorado. They believe the location will be better for James health and had plans to do truck farming to make a living. After several weeks, they re
2 CONC turned back to Conway stating that the location change didn't help, it was too dusty and they just didn't like it there.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1910 census shows the family living in Conway Springs, no street name given, may have been on a farm south west of Conway by this time.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1920 census, age 62 and truck farming in Conway Springs.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1930 census, back in town, owns own home worth $2,500, does not own a radio set, can read and write.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1931, passes away. No obit found to date.
