1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary published in The Gospel Messenger, March 7, 1914, page 158:
2 CONT
2 CONT Eubank, Sister Elizabeth Meda, youngest daughter of George and Sarah Obenchain, born in Lawrence County, Ill., May 26, 1892, died Feb. 14, 1914, at her mother’s home in Allison, Ill., aged 21 years, 8 months and 18 days. She marri
2 CONC ed Marion Eubank Oct. 7, 1911. She united with the church at the age of sixteen years and lived a consistent life. She leaves a husband, mother, one sister, two brothers and one half-brother. Services in the church at Allison Prai
2 CONC rie by Eld. O. B. Redenbo, assisted by Eld. J. C. Stoner, of Palestine. Text, Dan. 12: 2, 3. Interment in the cemetery near by. – Sadie Redenbo, R. D. 2. Lawrenceville, Ill.
