1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charles Edward “Bird” Obenchain rode with King Fisher and his gang in south Texas in the early 1870s. He apparently was a bit bloodthirsty. Supposedly, Obenchain (operating under an alias) tracked an enemy from Kan
2 CONC sas to south Texas, intending to kill the man. He ultimately caught up with the man. Obenchain allowed the doomed man to have a last meal—in fact, Bird had something to eat as well. When they finished, Bird shot the man down in co
2 CONC ld blood and left.
