1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nettle Welton
2 CONT      Services for Mrs. Nettie Welton, 94, of 1200 Vermont, who died Friday at a Boise nursing home, will be conducted at 3 p.m. Tuesday at Relyea Chapel by Pastor Robert Ballard of the Church of Christ. Interment will follow at Cl
2 CONC overdale.
2 CONT      Born Oct. 25, 1873, in Laramie County, Colo., she came by wagon train from Colorado to Oregon in 1878 and lived there until 1880 when she moved to the Wood River, Halley and Bellevue areas. On Nov. 30, 1916, she was married t
2 CONC o John H. Welton in Boise. She had lived in Boise for the past 70 years.
2 CONT      Mrs. Welton was a member of the Second United Presbyterian Church of Boise and was a member for 40 years of Aerie No. 115, Fraternal Order of Eagles.
2 CONT      Surviving are a granddaughter, Mrs. Helen Turner of Boise ; a grandson, William E. Flagler of Petaluma, Calif., seven great-grandchildren and five great-great-grandchildren.
2 CONT      Active pallbearers will be Mervin Kealey and James, Fred, John, Mark and Phil Obenchain all great-nephews of Mrs. Welton. Honorary pallbearers will be Guy, Alford and Robert Obenchain, Vernon Lee, John, Mike and Vernard Compt
2 CONC on and J. W. Brobeck.
2 CONT
2 CONT Idaho Daily Statesman, Monday, September 9, 1968
