1 TITL Dr
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dr. Clarence Philip Obenschain, Staunton physician, died suddenly Tuesday morning at his home "Selma."
2 CONT
2 CONT Born at Vinton, Sept. 10, 1878, he was a son of the Rev. James Patterson Obenschain and Sara F. Engleman Obenschain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Obenschain was educated at Washington and Lee University; was graduated from the Medical College of Virginia in 1904, and began the practice of medicine in Rockbridge County. He later moved to New Hope, remaining there until 1
2 CONC 928 where he established his practice in Staunton, and continuing until his retirement in 1945.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Obenschain served as Augusta County coroner for a number of years and in World War I was a captain in the Army Medical Corps. At the time of his death he held the rank of colonel in the Reserve Corps.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was an active member of Christ Lutheran Church, and for many years a member of the church council.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Obenschain is survived by his wife, Alice Kirkpatrick Obenschain; a sister, Eunice M. Obenschain, Washington; six sons, Claude of Washington; Dr. John T., Waynesboro; C. Philip Jr., Samuel., Richard O., and William B., Staunto
2 CONC n; four daughters, Mrs. Alvin E. Davis, Washington; Mrs. William W. McAllister, Waynesboro; Mrs. Walter F. Spitler, and Dr. Margaret B. Obenschain, Staunton. Twenty grandchildren also survive.
2 CONT
2 CONT A funeral will be conducted this afternoon at two o'clock from Christ Lutheran Church, the Rev. Melvin S. Lange officiating. Burial will be at Thornrose Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Active pallbearers will be: Dr. R. P. Bell Sr., G. Blosser, Dr. Kenneth Bradford, Dr. Glenn C. Campbell, Dr. Guy R. Fisher, Dr. S. H. Garst, F. C. Hamer, George V. La-Bonte, Dr. Alex F. Robertson, and Frank K. Shafer.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been requested that flowers be omitted. It is the desire of the family that those wishing to send flowers make a memorial gift to the King's Daughters' Hospital Building fund.
2 CONT
2 CONT The News Leader
2 CONT Staunton, Virginia
2 CONT 30 Nov 1949
