1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Paul was a minister in the Methodist Clergymd 1)  5 Aug 1873 Penelope Doramd 2) 27 Jun 1876 Cabell, WV to Sarah Ellen KenanPaul was the only member of his family that didn't initially move to Whiteside Co, Illinois
2 CONC  from VA/WV.  He and his brother Nathan changed the spelling of their name to reflect the ancestral spelling taken from cousins who also moved to Kentucky. His brother Athey later in life changed his to Hoffman as well.  The child
2 CONC ren erected the parents monument in the name of Hoffman, his father had signed his name Huffman.  Paul had no children of his own, nor did any of his 4 other brothers.  Paul & Sarah adopted a son, George W Hoffman who also became 
2 CONC a Reverend.Paul wrote the obituary for his sister Naomi which can be found through the family links first to Michael and then to Naomi.Many thanks go to Judi Fryer, ROAGK volunteer who located and took the family tombstone photos 
