1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Pvt Morgan Rexroad BIRTH	1832 Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA DEATH	18 Jun 1864 (aged 31–32) Lynchburg City, Virginia, USA BURIAL	 Poplar Grove National Cemetery Dinwiddie County, Virginia,
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/64351582/morgan-rexroad
2 CONT
2 CONT Morgan was the son of Zachariah Rexroad, Jr. and Sara Huffman. Morgan Rexroad was a Private in the Union Army, 11th WV Infantry, Company "C".He was mustered into service on August 11, 1863. He was killed in action on Saturday, Jun
2 CONC e 18, 1864 at the Battle of Lynchburg. He was 31 years old when he died. He was born prior to August 17, 1832 because according to the WV 1850 census on that date, he was 18 yrs. old. Further research indicates that he most likely
2 CONC  was originally buried on the Sandusky Estate land where a battle took place. Sandusky is a pre-Civil War home near Lynchburg, VA. It is believed that he was one of 10 unidentified Union Soldiers later moved and re buried at Popla
2 CONC r Grove Cemetery in Petersburg.
