3 STAE West Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 31 JUL 1914
1 OCCU Co. K, 25th Regiment, Virginia Infantry (Heck's)
1 TITL Pvt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacob J. Eye, section 4, is a native of Pendleton County, West Virginia, and was born October 20, 1840. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was brought up in the occupation of farming, and continued it at his birthplace till March, 1870, when he came to Missouri, locating in Henry County, near the St. Clair County line. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1872, he settled on his present farm. He has a fine tract of 282 acres, well improved. Mr. Eye was married May 10, 1862, to Miss F. Davis, who came originally from West Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They have eight children: Mary P., Floyd D., Ulra C., Jacob F., Robert L., James V., Gertie M., and an infant. Mr. E. was a soldier in Company K, Twenty-fifth Virginia Regiment, and served through the war.
2 CONT
2 CONT HISTORY OF ST. CLAIR COUNTY, MISSOURI 1883, information provided by T. J. Cockran
2 CONT
