1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hannah Hawes Trumbo BIRTH	12 May 1755 Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA DEATH	22 Feb 1852 (aged 96) Fort Seybert, Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA BURIAL	 Trumbo-May Cemetery #37 Pendleton County, West Virgi
2 CONC nia,
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/82313379/hannah-trumbo
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Hawes was the daughter of Henry Hawes and Sarah Dyer, daughter of Roger Dyer and his wife Hannah. Sarah was kidnapped by the Indians during the Fort Seybert massacre in April 1758 and did not return home for several years. 
2 CONC Hannah's father died or was killed between her birth and the date of the massacre. It is assumed, based on a court document of May 1758 that she lived with the Dyer family until she married George Cowger about 1777. After George d
2 CONC ied she married Jacob Trumbo about 1790 and lived in Brock gap. She is buried in the May cemetery. Following the massacre in 1758, Matthew Patton became guardian of Hannah, court records for May 15, 1758 show that Matthew being ap
2 CONC pointed guardian. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/m/i/l/Dennis-Stewart-Miller/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0022.html].
