1 NOTE {geni:about_me}     Isaac Newton LANGSTON, Robert PATTON Jr., Dorn PATTON, Andrew PATTON, and John McCAULEY purchased land at the Old Huntsville Land Office in 1818. This was in Morgan County, Alabama.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Patton Lineages Originating in Pennsylvania Prior to the Revolution" by David V. Agricola, MD, Cleveland Ohio, 1999:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Robert Patton was born perhaps around 1747, possibly in Sadsbury
2 CONT
2 CONT     Twp, Chester County, Penna. the names of his parents are
2 CONT
2 CONT     unknown, but evidence...suggests that he is a brother to John
2 CONT
2 CONT     PATTON, blacksmith (will 1800 Rowan Co.). Robert was living in
2 CONT
2 CONT     North Carolina prior to 1776, as he had a son, Robert Jr., born
2 CONT
2 CONT     there ca 1776. He married Jane (Dorrington)? ca. 1775. His
2 CONT
2 CONT     wife's maiden name is unknown, but as they had a son named
2 CONT
2 CONT     Dorrington (Dorn) it seems very possible that he was named after
2 CONT
2 CONT     his mother's family. On 8 Oct, 1776, Robert PATTON purchased
2 CONT
2 CONT     250 acres on the north branch of Cathey's Creek from Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT     THOMPSON (Tryon deed book 2:254)... Since Robert was living
2 CONT
2 CONT     very close to John PATTON (blacksmith) it seems very likely he
2 CONT
2 CONT     was the uncle of Joseph PATTON, who deposed that during the RW
2 CONT
2 CONT     (Revolutionary War) he had helped his uncle Robert, brother of
2 CONT
2 CONT     his father, who did blacksmith work under contract with the
2 CONT
2 CONT     army...."
2 CONT
2 CONT     "On 9 June 1778 Robert entered 640 acres on the waters of
2 CONT
2 CONT     Withrow's Creek adjoining Alexander McCorkle's; this land was
2 CONT
2 CONT     located just across the border of what would become Iredell Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT     in 1788.... State Land Grant #1317 was issued to him on 25 Oct
2 CONT
2 CONT     1786 (Entry book 326, book 67, p. 95)..."
2 CONT
2 CONT     In the 1790 Census there is one Robert PATTON in Iredell Co
2 CONT
2 CONT     (NC)...Robert had 3 males under 21 and 5 females, which matches
2 CONT
2 CONT     the family structure of Robert (d. 1813 TN)....On 6 Oct 1794
2 CONT
2 CONT     Robert sold the 320 acres tract on Withrow's Creek...presumably
2 CONT
2 CONT     in preparation for relocation."
2 CONT
2 CONT     Robert appears to have moved to Clark Co, Ky. in or about
2 CONT
2 CONT     October of 1794, there 1794-96 (tax lists)... In 1797 Montgomery
2 CONT
2 CONT     Co, Ky was formed out of part of Clark Co; Robert was on the tax
2 CONT
2 CONT     lists there 1797-1806 (but is not in the 1810 Census).... In the
2 CONT
2 CONT     period 1807-1811 Robert may have been in the part of Williamson
2 CONT
2 CONT     Co Tenn that in 1809 became the western part of Lincoln Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT     March 1811, Robert PATTON Sr. is one of the viewers to mark off
2 CONT
2 CONT     a road from Fayetteville, Lincoln Co Tenn..."
2 CONT
2 CONT     20 Sep 1813 is given as the date Robert Sr. died. After his
2 CONT
2 CONT     death the Lincoln Co. commissioners were appointed to design and
2 CONT
2 CONT     lay off a third portion of the 105 acres that Robert had owned
2 CONT
2 CONT     as the widow's portion for Jane PATTON, who served as the
2 CONT
2 CONT     administratrix."
2 CONT
2 CONT     <nowiki>------------------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT     Robert PATTON and family were in North Carolina prior to 1794 as
2 CONT
2 CONT     evidenced by the 1850 Census (Robert PATTON Jr. shown as born in
2 CONT
2 CONT     North Carolina). Dorn PATTON also shown as born in North
2 CONT
2 CONT     Carolina. In 1794, Robert PATTON appears in the Tax List for
2 CONT
2 CONT     Clark County, Kentucky, and remain there through 1796. In 1797
2 CONT
2 CONT     Robert PATTON appears in the Tax List for Montgomery County,
2 CONT
2 CONT     Kentucky, and remains there (as evidenced in Tax Lists) through
2 CONT
2 CONT     1806. from: Notes from Sandra P. McDaniel "Calendar", p. 1.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Family Migration: NC--KY--TN--AL
2 CONT
2 CONT     <nowiki>---------------------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT     May have had a brother named James PATTON: a James PATTON was
2 CONT
2 CONT     married to Polly HANSFORD, 16 Dec 1806 by Rev Joseph P. Howe in
2 CONT
2 CONT     Montgomery County, Kentucky. Rev Howe also preached in James
2 CONT
2 CONT     PATTON home during 1819.
2 CONT
2 CONT     <nowiki>----------------------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT     No record found showing where he was between 1806 and 1811.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Robert PATTON and family are not in Montgomery County, Kentucky
2 CONT
2 CONT     in the 1810 Census.
2 CONT
2 CONT     <nowiki>---------------------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT     Owned 2 plots of land (30 ac and 74 ac) in Lincoln County,
2 CONT
2 CONT     Tennessee 1811-1813.
2 CONT
2 CONT     <nowiki>----------------------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT     Research Notes: 1759 Rowan County, North Carolina Tax List shows
2 CONT
2 CONT     Robert PATTON along with James and Elijah.
2 CONT
2 CONT     "This tax list was found between the walls of the old court
2 CONT
2 CONT     house by Wm. D. Kizziah, Register of Deeds. When found, it was
2 CONT
2 CONT     but scraps of paper, but was fitted together and transcribed by
2 CONT
2 CONT     him. This list was made before Rowan Co, NC was divided into
2 CONT
2 CONT     other counties and is the oldest tax list ever found in
2 CONT
2 CONT     Rowan..."
2 CONT
2 CONT     IREDELL Co NC deed bk. B: p. 781 via Dr. David Agricola's
2 CONT
2 CONT     PATTON Internet pages, abstract follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT     6 Oct 1794 between Robert Patton of Iredell of one part and
2 CONT
2 CONT     Charles Mills of Rowan of second part- Robert in consideration
2 CONT
2 CONT     of 270 pounds paid by Mills ... sells a tract of land in Iredell
2 CONT
2 CONT     on both sides of Withrows Creek it being the the west and of ..
2 CONT
2 CONT     of land obtained by James Holmes from the office of said State,
2 CONT
2 CONT     by grant no. 489? and dated Oct 10th 1783, from thence conveyed
2 CONT
2 CONT     to Robert Patton by deed dated Jan. the 19th 1787 .. Beginning
2 CONT
2 CONT     at a [post?] in the original line ofsd. tract corner to Robert
2 CONT
2 CONT     Ramsey runs? west 140 poles to wh oak, then south th[ree]
2 CONT
2 CONT     hundred 66 poles to black oak, then East 140 poles to a hickory,
2 CONT
2 CONT     Robert Ramsey's corner, then along said Ramsey's line to a
2 CONT
2 CONT     spring thence the same course to a post oak nigh the creek
2 CONT
2 CONT     thence along the line to the beginning containing 320 acres more
2 CONT
2 CONT     or less; the other tract in the county and state afsd. on the
2 CONT
2 CONT     waters of Withrow's Creek it being a tract obtained by James
2 CONT
2 CONT     ....[Adams???] from the State by grant no. 139 and dated March
2 CONT
2 CONT     the 21st 1780, from thence conveyed to Robert Patton by deed
2 CONT
2 CONT     dated Jan 19th, 1787... beginning at a black oak thence south
2 CONT
2 CONT     200 poles to a post oak thence east 91 poles to a black oak
2 CONT
2 CONT     thence north 27 degrees east 58 poles to a white oak, thence to
2 CONT
2 CONT     the beginning, containing 110 acres more or less...
2 CONT
2 CONT     Signed Sealed and delivered in presents of wit- Robert McCorkle
2 CONT
2 CONT     Robert Patton (seal)
2 CONT
2 CONT     Robert Ramsey
2 CONT
2 CONT     Dec 27th 1797 Joseph McKay November session 1797- duly
2 CONT
2 CONT     executed... (no wife signed- at this time few deeds in Iredell
2 CONT
2 CONT     required this)
2 CONT
2 CONT     NOTE: This shows Robert PATTON to be in Iredell County, North
2 CONT
2 CONT     Carolina from at least January, 1787 through October, 1794.
2 CONT
2 CONT     NOTE: Withrow Creek coordinates: 354208N 0803629W (near Rowan
2 CONT
2 CONT     Mills).
2 CONT
