1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Will: 15 Feb 1834 Montgomery Co., VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT He is listed as a buyer in the Philip Barger sale of estate on October 21, 1802 in Montgomery Co., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Philip2 Keister  Jr. and an unknown spouse were as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT               7.          i.     Marathana3; born November 8, 1778.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT               8.          ii.     Polly; born circa 1780. [6]  Polly may be Marathana’s nickname.  Polly is listed as daughter in Philip Jr.’s will but Marathana is not.
2 CONT
2 CONT               9.        iii.     Elizabeth “BETSY”; born October 21, 1786; married Philip Bumgardner September 6, 1804 in Montgomery Co., VA.[7],[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT +          10.         iv.     John, born October 16, 1789; married Sarah Martin.
2 CONT
2 CONT             11.         v.     George; born January 27, 1794 in VA;[9],[10] married Christina Walters circa 1820; died after 1860.[11]
2 CONT
2 CONT      He was a farmer in 1855 in Montgomery Co., VA.[12] A male slave was born on the Keister farm.  Possibly this was a different George Keister.  This one is most likely because he was the most wealthy on April 10, 1855 in Montgo
2 CONC mery Co., VA.[13] He lived in 1860 in Montgomery Co., VA and owned $5000 in real estate and $1750 in personal property.[14]
2 CONT
2 CONT             12.         vi.     Susanna; born August 4, 1799;[15] married Isaac Henderliter August 25, 1825 in Montgomery County, VA
