2 CONT Albemarle County Deed Book, 1793-1795
2 CONT
2 CONT pg 228
2 CONT
2 CONT Kesiter to Kesiter, Deed
2 CONT Know all men by those presents that I John Kesiter and Feronica
2 CONT Keister, Wife of the said John Keister, and the lawful daughter of
2 CONT Leonard Toolewiler, both of the County of Albemarle for divers good
2 CONT causes and considerations as thereunto moving have and by  these presents
2 CONT do constitute and appoint our true and trusty friend and honored
2 CONT Father, Phillip Kesiter of Rockingham County our true and  lawful Attorney for
2 CONT us and in our names to settle with Jacob Toolewiler of County ofWashington
2 CONT and state  of Maryland, Executor of Henry Toolewiler, deceased, all
2 CONT Accounts with regards to his executorship so far as touching the right
2 CONT of the said Feronica Kesiter's Legacy left to her by the Last Will and Testament of
2 CONT Henry Toolewiler and upon settlement thereof to ask demand sue for the
2 CONT recover and from Jacob Toolerwiler any money or monies that may be due to her,
2 CONT the said Feronica Keister, on account of the Estate of her Uncle Henry Toolewiler ,
2 CONT deceased and upon receipt thereof proper acquittance's or  other discharges made and deliver in our or either of our names and to actin all respects as fully in the premises
2 CONT as we ourselves could do were we personally present hereby ratifyingan d
2 CONT confirming whatsoever our Attorney shall lawfully do in the premises,I n Witness
