1 NAME Martha Rebecca /Cowger/
2 GIVN Martha Rebecca
2 SURN Cowger
2 _MARNM Bodkin
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Union Cemetery, Brookfield Township, Clinton County, Iowa, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 20 OCT 1844
2 PLAC Pendleton County, West Virginia, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE APR 1919
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The funeral of the late Mrs. William Bodkin, who passed away at her home in the Scott rooming house, Saturday morning, was held from the home Monday afternoon, Rev. J. J. Kidder officiating.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha R. Cowger was born at Sweedlin Hill, Pendelton County, West Virginia, October 20, 1844, and was united in marriage to William Bodkin, March 1, 1866, they coming to Iowa in 1869 and locating in Clinton County, where after  r
2 CONC emaining a short time they removed to a farm two and a half miles southwest of Maquoketa, residing there twenty-seven years when they removed to  Maquoketa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Bodkin passed away April 21, 1912. To this union seven children were born, one son passing away in infancy, and another son, George, on  December 10, 1918. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Those surviving are Jack of Muscatine, Howard, Henry, and Mrs. Fortis Current of Maquoketa and Anna of home. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased united with the Methodist Church when quite young and was a faithful member until death. In early days her West Virginia home was located on the boundary line between the north and south, and one of her chief enjoyments w
2 CONC as  to converse with her old Virginia friends, recalling the many stirring incidents of the civil war. She was a faithful wife and a kind mother and highly respected in the community which for so many years had been her home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment was made in the Union Cemetery south of Maquoketa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jackson Sentinel, Maquoketa, Iowa, April 5, 1919* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/127966456/martha-rebecca-bodkin Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 20 2020, 2
