2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 JAN 1951
2 PLAC Palo Alto, Santa Clara County, California, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry Jacob and John Pendleton Cowger were twins. Henry married Susanna "Sudie" Christina Harper on 18 June 1885 in Pendleton County, West Virginia.  Susanna was much taller than Henry.  Their first child, John Les
2 CONC ter, was born in Moorefield, WV. Henry may have been a deputy sheriff in Elkins, WV, for a while.   In 1888 the young family  took a train west, ending up in King City, California.  A daughter, Bessie Pearl, was born there in 1889
2 CONC .  In April 1890 the growing family moved northwest to Salinas to join Susanna's brother, John Michael Harper and his wife, Clara.  John ran a grocery in Salinas and Henry replaced John's former partner.  A month after the move, B
2 CONC essie died. In 1891, Henry and Susanna's second daughter, Hazel Dare, arrived. Two years later, John Harper died and his widow, Clara, returned east with her four children. In Feb 1895 Henry and Susanna are living in Pacific Grove
2 CONC , on the California coast, where Henry opens a hardware store.  A month later, their second son, Harold "Lefty" Victor Cowger, was born. In July 1897 the family is back in King City where their last child, Winslow Llewellyn Cowger
2 CONC , was born. 1900 census records show the family in West Virginia but by 1910 they are back in California, living in San Jose.  This is when San Jose was known for its citrus orchards.  In 1930, Henry was retired and he and Susanna
2 CONC  lived in Palo Alto. Prior to Henry's death at age 90, he and his brother, John, believed themselves the oldest twins in the United States.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/195925625/henry-jacob-cowger Find A Grave
2 CONC  Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 20 2020, 2:00:29 UTC''
