1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/54013244/john-pendleton-cowger
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pendlton Cowger was born in Ft. Seybert, West Virginia to Jesse and Polly Ann Keister Cowger.  He Married Mary Elvira Hevener on Dec. 4, 1884 in Franklin, WV.  John and Mary had the following children: Henry Casper, Charles W
2 CONC hitfield, Bessie Mae, Ethel Lynn, William Parron, Lola Vida, Emma Jane, Frederick, and Iva Elizabeth.  John lived to be 97 and was in good health.  The family story is that two boys beat and robbed him.  He was known to be a "Hors
2 CONC e Trader".  I was told that he would come to town with one or two knives and return home with a pocketful.  He could often be seen sitting in town whittling and making canes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dancing at Byrd's Restaurant A resident of Franklin shared the following story about John Cowger. "Once you got a couple of beers in old man John, he would get up on the counter and dance.  He was wanting to dance one day, so they
2 CONC  moved the juke box in the back and he was dancing.  Next thing I know he cut a sumersault and landed.  Well he couldn't get back up.  We just knew he was hurt bad.  We'll, they helped him back to his feet and darned if he didn't 
2 CONC pop back up and start dancing again.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/54013244/john-pendleton-cowger Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 20 2020, 2:00:29 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/54013244/john-pendleton-cowger
