2 CONT Barbara Sarah Fisher formerly Coil Born 17 Jan 1778 in Augusta, Virginia, United States Ancestors  Daughter of George Coil and Maria Johannah (Hevener) Coil  Sister of Catherine Coil, Georg Coil, Mary Hannah (Coil) Mullenax and Ma
2 CONC ria Elizabetha (Coil) Sinnett  Wife of Jacob Fisher — married about 1796 [location unknown]  Descendants  Mother of John Fisher, Catherine Fisher and Jacob Fisher Jr  Died 11 Apr 1855 in Ross, Ohio, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography  Barbara Sarah Coil (17 JAN 1778 Augusta County, Virginia - now Pendleton, West Virginia - 11 APR 1855 Concord, Ross, Ohio) was the daughter of George Coil (1730–1794) and Maria Johanna Hevener (1747–1837). 
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1796 in Pendelton, Virginia (now West Virginia) she married Jacob Fisher. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:  John Fisher (26 Nov 1797 Pennsylvania - 26 Aug 1853 buried Ross County, Ohio) married Phebe Briggs (1790 Virginia - 4 Mar 1864 Ross County, Ohio)  Hannah Fisher (16 Jan 1803 - 14 Dec 1840 Ross County, Ohio) married Mary
2 CONC  Ridgeway  Absalom Fisher ( Jun 1805 Ross County, Ohio - 11 Feb1843 Ross County, Ohio) married Elizabeth Hughes  Phoebe Fisher ( 1807 – 1829 Ross County, Ohio)  Susan Fisher (30 Aug 1810 Ross County, Ohio - 19 Sep 1886 Ross County
2 CONC , Ohio) married John Maddux  Catherine Fisher (24 Mar 1813 Ross, Ohio - 30 DEC 1896 Barry, Pike, Illinois) married Abiah Wright (1 NOV 1809 Rostraver, Westmoreland, Pennsylvania - 13 Mar 1884 Barry, Pike, Illinois) and had 11 chil
2 CONC dren.[1]  Willomina Fisher (1816–1844) married David T. Harper  Jacob Jack Fisher 1819–1897 (Feb. 23, 1819 - 12 Apr 1897 Ross County, Ohio) married Eleanor Wilson.  Adam Clements Fisher 1820–1889 
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary:  Barbara Ann Coile Fisher; wife of Jacob Fisher, born in what is now Pendleton County (formerly part of Augusta County Virginia), West Virginia. Dau of George and Hannah Coile. Ch: John, Hannah, Phillip, Absalom, Phebe, 
2 CONC Susan, Catherine, Willomenia, and Jacob, Jr.  Burial[2]: Concord Presbyterian Church Cemetery; Lattaville, Ross County, Ohio 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes:  1820 [3] Ross, Ohio with husband Jacob Fisher  1830[4]: Concord, Ross, Ohio, United States. Jacob Fisher  1840[5] Concord Township, Ross, Ohio; Jacob Fisher and family  1850[6] Concord, Ross, Ohio. Barbara Fisher, Age 75, 
2 CONC Birth Year abt 1775, with husband Jacob Fisher 77 born in Pennsylvania and Margaret Fisher 11 (granddaughter?)  1860[7]: Concord, Ross, Ohio. Jacob Fisher, Age 86, Birth Year abt 1774, Birthplace: Virginia, living with Zachariah H
2 CONC  Figen age 26 and his family, relationship unknown. 
