1 NOTE In 1738, Adam Miller, Jr. and Catharine Miller, children of Adam, Sr. were baptized by Rev. John Casper Stover, Lutheran minister at Hebron Church in Madison County, Virginia, 1733-39.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1765 Henry Miller and Jacob Baer were elders at St. Peters.  There may have been other children of Adam Miller.
2 CONT
2 CONT A short distance south of Bear Lithea Springs is an old cemetery with at least 3 well-preserved sandstones standing.  The author, Harry M. Strickler, visited in 1931.  The stones are 18 inches high, 12 inches wide and 6 inches thi
2 CONC ck; the lettering is deeply cut in German letters, at least the two older stones are, and each has a biblical quotation to cover the entire stone.  Facing west and reading from left to right, they are Jacob Bear, departed this lif
2 CONC e 17 May 1827, age 61 yrs 5 mos & 17 days.  Footstone is marked JB3.
2 CONT
2 CONT Next is Jacob Bear 1724 - 1783 ?(the last figure being indistinct); Barbara Bearin (the in on end of name indicated wife) born 1726-1791. This is daughter of Adam Miller, who married Jacob Bear, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Augusta County book listing marriages between 1748 and 1850, there are over 2 pages of Miller marriages.  I listed only the ones I had information on previously.
