1 NOTE {geni:about_me} George McNaught Bartholomew was the son of Major General Joseph Bartholomew and his wife Elizabeth McNaught Bartholomew.
2 CONT
2 CONT From "The History of Columbia County, Wisconsin" 1880:
2 CONT
2 CONT G.M. BARTHOLOMEW, retired farmer, Lodi; born in Clarke Co., Ind., in 1812, where he lived till he was 21 years of age, when he removed to McLean Co., Ill., where he lived till April, 1845, when he came to the town of Lodi, and set
2 CONC tled on Sec. 26, where he engaged in farming; Mr. Bartholomew is also a surveyor, and has been engaged in that occupation more or less for many years; in 1875, Mr. B. retired from farming, and has since resided in the village of L
2 CONC odi. His wife was Miss S. C. Hefner, born in Virginia; they have seven children-C. Elizabeth, now Mrs. James McCloud; B. Jane, now Mrs. George Cleghorn, resides in Nebraska; Joseph M., by profession a lawyer, of Red Oak, Iowa; Mar
2 CONC y A., now Mrs. E. B. Wait; Josephine, now Mrs. W. H. Chapin, resides in Nebraska: Ellen, wife of L. K. Luse, Esq., of Dane Co., and James I., a student at Lawrence University. Mr. Bartholomew has been Justice of the Peace for twen
2 CONC ty years.
