1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jeremiah was the son of James Thornton Dean and his first wife, Susannah Harness. Susannah died from influenza when Jeremiah was small. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the book, The Dean Mountain Story, by Gloria Dean (Appalachian Trail Club, 1982)* Jeremiah left Dean Mountain, at the age of 17, and settled in the area of Swift Run Gap, near Stanardsville, in Greene County Va., and 
2 CONC married Lucretia Haney. They had 10 children together and Jeremiah died at 47 years of age. He was apparently buried at the family home at Swift Run Gap. *However, it should be noted that many of the details in this book in regard
2 CONC s  to  James Dean's first family are either incorrect or fiction.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Lucretia Haney and Jeremiah M. Deane, Sr., were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy C (Knight, Donovan) 1841 – 1872
2 CONT James William 1842 – 1900
2 CONT Elizabeth Agnes (Shiflett) 1849 – 
2 CONT Matthew 1851 – 
2 CONT Sarah (Offield) 1853 – 
2 CONT Lucindy "Sandi" (Breeden, Donovan) 1854 – 1900
2 CONT Jeremiah M., Jr. 1856 – 1901
2 CONT Loucetta S (Knight) 1859 – 1939
2 CONT Martha J 1860 – 
2 CONT Andrew Jackson 1861 – 1933* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/43111090/jeremiah-monroe-deane Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 5 2024, 19:10:52 UTC''
