1 NAME James Harvey /Kesling/
2 GIVN James Harvey
2 _MARNM Kesling
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 MAY 1804
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 AUG 1891
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L4WZ-GSY
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary: "James Kesling was born October 29, 1804 was converted in early life, joined M.E. Chruch was married to Mary Wamsley, June 1823.
2 CONT
2 CONT They raised seven children, four sons and three girls, three of seven have gone (to) the world of eternity. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Kesling can truly be called the planter and cultivator of Methodism in his community. Before the church had an organization in his community or a house in which to worship, a log church was built on his land and Bro. Keslin
2 CONC g lived to see the old Log church worn out, and a neat frame erected in its stead. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 2nd day of August 1891, in his 87th year, God sent the release Angel to deliver this man of God from his suffering. He is buried in the Kesling Cemetery beside his wife (son of Jacob and Mary Black Kesling),"
2 CONT
2 CONT James Harvey Kesling 
