1 NOTE {geni:about_me} OBITUARY
2 CONT RAY BRENNARD DEAN, 63, OF 121 Martin St., a retired employe of the Continental Can Co., with 37 years of service, died Thursday at 6:55 p.m. in a local hospital followin an extended illness.  He was born Jan. 29, 1907 in Upshur Co
2 CONC unty, the son of the late Arch and Rebecca Frances Jack Dean.  Surviving are his widow, Golida I. Coffindaffer; one son Ray B. Dean, Jr. of Portage, Ind; two daughters, Mrs. James (Virginia) Beverly of 336 Point St., and Mrs. Rich
2 CONC ard R (Shirley)Taylor of Medina,Ohio; three brothers, W.Dexter Dean, Buckhannon, U.Grant Dean, of Clarksburg; and the Rev. Virgil Dean of Fairmont, four sisters, Mrs. Ima McIntyre, Mrs. Paul (Georgia ) Smith of Akron, Ohio, Mrs. B
2 CONC retsel (Wanita) Gainor of Clarksburg and Mrs. Ruth Nesbitt of Elkins, 11 grandchildren.  He was preceded in death by two brothers and three sisters.  Mr. Dean was a member of the Broad Oaks United Methodist Church* Reference: [htt
2 CONC ps://www.findagrave.com/memorial/37358506/ray-brennard-dean Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 1 2023, 5:34:52 UTC''
