1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Logging Mishap Kills Upshur Man
2 CONT Buckhannon, W.Va. (AP)
2 CONT
2 CONT An Upshur County contractor and carpenter was killed Thursday when a load of timber overturned on him after he had been cutting fire wood.
2 CONT
2 CONT State Police identified the victim as Dexter Dean, 50, of Kesling Mill near here.
2 CONT
2 CONT They said Dean and Archie White had been cutting the timber on a farm owned by Lynn Westfall.  After loading the logs on a wagon pulled by a tractor, the two proceeded down a steep hill when the tongue on the wagon broke causing i
2 CONC t to overturn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Authorities said Dean, who was standing atop the logs, was thrown to the ground and crushed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dexter William Dean
2 CONT Buckhannon-Dexter William Dean, 55, of Route 4, died at 10 a.m. Dec 30 at the Russell Westfall farm on the Kesling Mill Road.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born Dec 18, 1916 in Upshur County, a son of the late Arch and Rebecca Jack Dean.
2 CONT
2 CONT Six brothers and sisters preceded him in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are his wife, Mrs. Margueritte Westfall Dean, Route 4; four sons, William David Dean, Clarksburg; Dwayne Paul, Route 1, Ralph Maymard, Route 4, and Gary Lynn Route 1; two daughters, Mrs. Joe (Margaret) Strough, Route 4, 
2 CONC and Deborah Dianna Dean, at home; two brothers, Grant Dean, Clarksburg, Rt.1 and The Rev. Virgil Dean, Fairmont, four sisters, Mrs. Ima McIntire and Mrs. Juanita Gainer, both of Clarksburg, Mrs. Georgia Smith, Akron, Ohio, and Mrs
2 CONC . Ruth Nesbitt, Elkins, and 13 grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a carpenter by trade and a member of the Kesling United Methodist Church* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/36999968/dexter-william-dean Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 
