1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Emogene Ruth Dean Nesbitt, age 89 years, a resident of Elkins, passed away Wednesday, January 14, 2015 at her home. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born May 9, 1925 in Buckhannon, the youngest child of the late Arch and Rebecca Jack Dean.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She grew up in the Kesling Mill area of Buckhannon and completed 8th grade in 1940 at the one room school at Kesling Mill.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She graduated from Buckhannon High School in 1944.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Ruth began working for C & P Telephone Company of Clarksburg in 1946 and married James Robert Nesbitt in 1952 moving to Oberlin, Ohio where she worked for Ohio Bell Company. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the next seven years, she lived in Dayton, Ohio, Kentucky and Indiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT  In 1958, she and Robert moved to Elkins where she was a Teller at the C & P Business Office, later worked at the Memorial General Hospital Admissions Office and was employed for ten years as a bookkeeper at Mary’s Greenhouse. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1975, she moved to Clarksburg where she worked at Parsons Sauders and Townhouse West Motel.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She returned to Elkins in 1992 and worked as a caregiver.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Ruth was a devoted mother, cherished sister, grandmother, great grandmother and beloved aunt and friend. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a shining example of the traditions and values instilled in her as a child by her family.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She had a strong work ethic on the job and at home.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She was a perfectionist who believed that a job worth doing was worth doing right. Her home, car and clothes were immaculate.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She had a “knack” for cleaning, painting and home improvements. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, her “green thumb” was the envy of many.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She loved flowers and managed to keep them healthy and thriving with her persistent care.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Her special touch carried over into her compassion for people. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She “adopted” many elderly people for whom she provided food, cleaning and a listening ear.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She also loved to collect owls and was proud of her collection of 450 owls.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She will be very much missed by those who were honored to know her. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her parents and husband, Ruth was preceded in death by six brothers, Winford, Donald, Ray, Grant, Dexter and Rev. Virgil Dean; six sisters, Alice, Frances and Dorothy Dean, Ima McIntire, Georgia Smith and Juanita Ga
2 CONC inor.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She is survived by one son, Richard Alan Nesbitt and wife Faye of Montrose, one daughter, Karen Hunt and husband Orval of Beverly, one grandson, J.R. Nesbitt of Elkins, a granddaughter, Veronica Isner and husband Chris, Elkins, o
2 CONC ne great granddaughter, Brooklynn Isner and special nieces, Dr. Patty Gaynor, Zanesville, OH, Margaret “Sis” Strouth and Debbie Rice both of Buckhannon and special nephews, Billy Gainor, Maidsville, WV and David, Dwayne and Gary D
2 CONC ean of Buckhannon.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She was the last surviving member of her immediate family of thirteen children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call from 6:00 pm until 8:00 pm Friday, January 16, 2015 at the Tomblyn Funeral Home in Elkins.
2 CONT
2 CONT  A funeral service will be held at 11:00 am Saturday, January 17th from the funeral home chapel with Pastor Joey Ridenour officiating. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment will follow in the Mt. Rupert Cemetery near Buckhannon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Tomblyn Funeral Home of Elkins is in charge of the arrangements for Emogene Ruth Dean Nesbitt.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Condolences may be expressed to the family at www.tomblynfuneralhome.com.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tomblyn Funeral Home - January 15, 2015* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/141380188/emogene-ruth-nesbitt Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 1 2023, 5:34:52 UTC'
